{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex","id":971363,"title":"Diablerie and Auspex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-17T09:44:17-07:00","id":971363,"title":"Diablerie and Auspex","content":"Diablerie is probably the most unaceptable crime among kindred society. I'm wondering about how long the tracks of diablerie are detectable through Auspex? Forever or just for the duration of the tainted condition? If the amaranth is always detectable hohard the life for the vampire should be? can you give me some advice about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:00:22-07:00","id":971368,"title":"","content":"Since the question is &quot;Is this person a Diablerist?&quot; and not some variant of &quot;Do they have the Tainted condition?&quot; I'd rule that you can always detect it.<br /> <br /> Some ways to make this less miserable for a Diablerist that I have heard in the past are as follows:<br /> <br /> 1. Many Domains make Diablerie legal in certain circumstances, such as the target of a Blood Hunt. I dislike this personally, since Diablerie is more than just murder. It's devouring a soul. I can't fathom vampires being okay with it ever, not even in special circumstances.<br /> <br /> 2. Without additional evidence, it's your word versus the accuser's. Nobody but another vampire with Auspex can corroborate the story. People are probably loathe to trust vampires with Auspex at their word without evidence because: you can't really be sure they even have Auspex without questioning them repeatedly on things they couldn't otherwise know, they could be lying even if they have Auspex, and supporting their accusations now could make them more credible if they come around and accuse you later. I prefer this explanation. Even if a Mekhet <i>knows </i>you are a Diablerist, that doesn't mean they can do anything about it or that anyone will believe them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:08:16-07:00","id":971371,"title":"","content":"I usually run it with Auspex 1 triggering a lot of 'Danger!' alerts when someone has the Tainted Condition, but when the marks are gone it goes back to normal, providing they've gotten over their addiction.<br /> <br /> Auspex 2, like Maina says, will always ping a yes on the direct question, but may no longer go directly to it for things like 'the worst thing they have done' or 'greatest secret.'<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32359-predatory-aura?p=32564#post32564\">Apparently there were some plans for further abilities to sniff out Diablerie taints.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:14:58-07:00","id":971378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=971368#post971368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the question is &quot;Is this person a Diablerist?&quot; and not some variant of &quot;Do they have the Tainted condition?&quot; I'd rule that you can always detect it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my interpretation as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=971368#post971368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some ways to make this less miserable for a Diablerist that I have heard in the past are as follows:<br /> <br /> 1. Many Domains make Diablerie legal in certain circumstances, such as the target of a Blood Hunt. I dislike this personally, since Diablerie is more than just murder. It's devouring a soul. I can't fathom vampires being okay with it ever, not even in special circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, this varies by domain. Some domains will see Diablerie as an unforgivable crime under any circumstances, others will sanction it only as the most dire of punishments, some will sanction it for petty or frivolous reasons. In one game I played, the Sheriff was a known diablerist, but was pardoned because he only diablerized other diablerists. In the same game, there was a character who the Prince declared didn't count as Kindred under her rule, and so was not protected by the Traditions. He probably would have been diablerized, but he had a Mage protecting him. That game was probably the most permissive towards Diablerie I've ever actually seen in play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=971368#post971368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Without additional evidence, it's your word versus the accuser's. Nobody but another vampire with Auspex can corroborate the story. People are probably loathe to trust vampires with Auspex at their word without evidence because: you can't really be sure they even have Auspex without questioning them repeatedly on things they couldn't otherwise know, they could be lying even if they have Auspex, and supporting their accusations now could make them more credible if they come around and accuse you later. I prefer this explanation. Even if a Mekhet <i>knows </i>you are a Diablerist, that doesn't mean they can do anything about it or that anyone will believe them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much how I treat it most of the time. And this doesn't just apply to Diablerie, Auspex is never admissible evidence in kindred court in my games, because it's very difficult to corroborate, and no one wants to give every Mekhet in the city the power to condemn anyone merely on their word. That's how witch hunts happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:22:32-07:00","id":971420,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the tips <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:23:14-07:00","id":971421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex#post971363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diablerie is probably the most unaceptable crime among kindred society. I'm wondering about how long the tracks of diablerie are detectable through Auspex?</div> </div> </div> </div> I personally say for the duration of the Tainted Condition; alternatively, if they're still addicted to Diablerie. The power is Aura Reading, not &quot;Past Crime Reading.&quot; If you're not Tainted or Addicted, then your aura has been cleaned out. No reason I can see to pick up somthing that's no longer there in one's aura. Granted, getting rid of the addiction is nearly impossible - there's a reason we say that someone is a recovering addict, not &quot;no longer an addict.&quot; But I can see excessive uses of torpor and some Disciplines that could work to that effect. <br /> <br /> But, really, the best answer to this question is &quot;What works best for your game?&quot; Maybe your Prince has Auspex, and given that she's the final authority anyways, can easily make a judgement on the matter. Or perhaps someone uses Dominate or Theban Sorcery to force the issue. So, in order for a certain plots with diablery to work, you need to have a certain way that all this works. Making broad, sweeping generalizations about this issue isn't really a good idea. <br /> <br /> Or, better yet? Deliberately leave the question unanswered and have the characters at a loss. They suspect this person committed diablerie. Auspex 2 says &quot;no.&quot; But, under Dominate, she says &quot;yes.&quot; Does Tainted have an effect? Was her memory twisted? Plausable Deniablity or one of the sorceries in play? Strix? Something else? Mysteries and doubt are a good thing, and leaving the answer open gives you more flexibility as an ST, while having no answer leads to better plot hooks as a player. There's doubt in the air. <i>What do you do?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:44:30-07:00","id":971426,"title":"","content":"Dramatic failure. Auspex is unreliable so I doubt it is used to officially cast guilt on someone. If the Prince says, &quot;By my power of Auspex, I declare that vampire a diablerist. Get 'em&quot; then everyone would probably start looking for a new Prince unless &quot;that vampire&quot; just happened to have lots of enemies. I think it should always be detectable by Auspex because diablerie addiction is both automatic and permanent, as are the benefits received from diablerie. It is the counterbalance.<br /> <br /> The life difficulties will be personal rather than societal. Some will fear or hate based on the rumors. Others will blow it off because even if it were true there are no circumstances to go with the charge. A person can be forgiven terrible deeds if their reason is good enough. Man A tortures then murders man B so man A must be evil. Except, man B raped, tortured and murdered man A's 5 year old child. Man A is not so bad anymore. Knowing a vampire is a diablerist is evidence that they are dangerous, but the vampire part should have done that already. I doubt most vampires go around fearing diablerie more than final death.<br /> <br /> Then there are the strix. Since a diablerist reads the same as a strix, I imagine they need to get out of town if a strix is known to be around. Nobody wants a third nipple when a witch hunt starts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:45:14-07:00","id":971427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=971421#post971421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I personally say for the duration of the Tainted Condition; alternatively, if they're still addicted to Diablerie. The power is Aura Reading, not &amp;quot;Past Crime Reading.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry it was my fault but I referred to 2 ed. In 2ed there isn't aura reading anymore. The power works differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:46:10-07:00","id":971467,"title":"","content":"They are sample questions so they can be taken, disregarded or altered. If someone has a problem with the question and rather it would be if a vampire has the Tainted condition due to diablerie, okay. That changes the view of the diablerist because the situation is different. Doesn't appear to me you are going that route, though, so I'll leave it at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:59:15-07:00","id":972621,"title":"","content":"I've never liked the combination of being able to detect diablerie by Auspex and it being some unpardonable act in vampire society. Either one alone would be fine, but put the two together and it's tremendously limiting in scenarios, campaigns and characters. Auspex 2 is easy to get and whilst people make brave attempts to rationalize why it isn't useful (how do you know you can trust the person with the Auspex), such efforts go pop far too easily (the Prince has Auspex, someone the Prince trusts more than you has Auspex, your coterie mate has Auspex, some random other vampire has Auspex and even though it's not proof, tells people that you're a diablerist and that's enough to make people not trust you, the prince finds another vampire to give a second opinion just like a doctor can check another doctor's work... and so on).<br /> <br /> It feels to me like something Mark Rein\u2022Hagen put in just to stop power-gaming players immediately setting about devouring all their elders. (Which to be fair, it works as). But imo, the number of plotlines and character choices that get shut down immediately by it, I prefer to make it so that it's not easily detectible. I think a lot of GMs tie themselves in knots trying to find reasons why a vampire with Auspex detecting it doesn't lead to a bloodhunt. Or else they end up with a setting where Diablerie becomes just a thing everyone accepts but nobody acknowledges. Like having watched a Michael Bay film.<br /> <br /> I prefer to just bite the bullet so to speak and say &quot;can't detect&quot;, or at least make it require some exceptional rolling so people are never sure if they might have missed it. Now I'm no longer faced with my campaign becoming an endless attempt to justify not killing a PC whose aura screams devilry; or trying to figure out how my diablerist elder can keep their secret from everyone. If thine auspex eye offends thee, pluck it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:07:45-07:00","id":972627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=971421#post971421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I personally say for the duration of the Tainted Condition; alternatively, if they're still addicted to Diablerie. The power is Aura Reading, not &quot;Past Crime Reading.&quot; If you're not Tainted or Addicted, then your aura has been cleaned out. No reason I can see to pick up somthing that's no longer there in one's aura. Granted, getting rid of the addiction is nearly impossible - there's a reason we say that someone is a recovering addict, not &quot;no longer an addict.&quot; But I can see excessive uses of torpor and some Disciplines that could work to that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. &quot;is this person a diablerist?&quot; Are they still addicted and or tainted? Do they still do it? Actively seeking out vampires or waiting for an opportune time? = Then my answer is yes.<br /> <br /> Did they do it 100 years ago? just one time and got over it after a long torpor or whatever? = Then no. They are not a diablerist. They did commit it once upon a time, but no longer fall to the urge. <br /> <br /> However if you asked, &quot;Has this person ever commit diablerie&quot;? Then my answer would be yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:39:53-07:00","id":972779,"title":"","content":"There are ways to dodge being found out. The first is to stake your target and wait for a bit before doing the deed so your disappearance doesn't coincide with the investigation, another is to agro the taint away and hope no one questions the scars.<br /> I personally would only allow players to detect a post Tainted diablerist on an exceptional success. It's worth pointing out that Strix read as &quot;a vampire who has committed diablerie.&quot; I don't know if helps one way or the other in the debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:01:12-07:00","id":972794,"title":"","content":"I'd like to simply point out that the tainted condition is at the same much less and much more harsh than in previous games. The time for its ellipse is much smaller that the years of classic. but at the same time a interesting mechanic is set in place. The victim trying to sabotage from the inside, is really cool and the thematic.<br /> <br /> I like to think a vamp with auspex, that figures out a dia has two different choices. Blackmail or avoidance. Its just more information and a heads up to danger. I can definitely imagine a Mehket trying to pick his fights. And once seeing the Dia under auspex, going &quot;OK not dealing with that&quot; and pawning off the fight to some unknowing vamp thinking he's getting a better deal. Effectively changing his plans to get a safer easier bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:30:27-07:00","id":972814,"title":"","content":"I was personally of the opinion it was only detectable for the duration of the tainted condition. <br /> <br /> The better to hide a real monster in the groups midst","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T19:34:18-07:00","id":972887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=972814#post972814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was personally of the opinion it was only detectable for the duration of the tainted condition.<br /> <br /> The better to hide a real monster in the groups midst</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically how I intend to run it. The tainted condition is kind of meaningless if diablerists are detectable as diablerists long after the condition has been resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T22:58:13-07:00","id":972948,"title":"","content":"Weak vampires that commit diablerie get dusted as they should. For those that are not weak, I think there is a view on diablerie that is slightly exaggerated. You can make something of a recent diablerie, but if it occurred long ago then problems can arise. Vampire society is hypocritical. Diablerie is the worst thing a vampire can do, worse than murder for mortals, but sometimes a Prince will order diablerie as a punishment, like some societies execute murderers. Would you really blackmail a hitman or serial killer? Do you tell the Prince a vampire is a diablerist but don't know the victim or how long ago it was? What if the Prince says, &quot;I know&quot;? Personally, if I was a Prince I was say, &quot;Okay, since you know, go deal with them.&quot; Whether I gave the diablerist a call would depend on which I liked better.<br /> <br /> I view vampire society like a prison with the vampires like prisoners, but I don't think everyone can relate so if I knew a diablerist I would give them a wide berth and try to avoid being vulnerable to the diablerist, certainly, but otherwise would leave them alone because unless you're Willie McCoy I say:<br /> <br /> You don't tug on Superman's cape<br /> You don't spit into the wind<br /> You don't pull the mask off that old Lone Ranger<br /> And you don't mess around with a diablerist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:23:58-07:00","id":972962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=972627#post972627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Has this person ever commit diablerie&quot;? Then my answer would be yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure this question would be legit with Auspex. I mean, if it would so you could also ask: &quot;Has this person killed/rape/rapt?&quot; But you can't ask for this kind of question (more suitable for Auspex 4), according to my interpretation at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T00:02:43-07:00","id":972970,"title":"","content":"Level 2 of Auspex is for unveiling secrets. That's (probably) a secret. Seems legit to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not sure why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2367_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2367\" data-vbnamecard=\"2367\">Resplendent Fire</a> thinks Tainted is &quot;meaningless&quot; if Diablerists can be detected when it wears off. The point isn't to mark a Diablerist. The point is to hammer home the thematic fact that Diablerie is devouring the soul of your victim. It's about personal horror, not getting caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T02:43:47-07:00","id":973008,"title":"","content":"Well not meaningless clearly, but perhaps I should say there's something wrong with &quot;you are a diablerist&quot; being eternally detectable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T04:56:17-07:00","id":973041,"title":"","content":"Not to mention there are other ways you could be put on to a diablerist after the taint wears off. <br /> <br /> In the political arena I'm sure a common question would be, what is this person's desire/goal?<br /> <br /> Another listed example would be: what is his psychological weakness?<br /> <br /> While not a definitive answer I would give players clues with other appropriate questions, while maintaining they are not, once the tainted condition has worn off. <br /> <br /> The personal horror for the player is the addiction. Even if they get away with it, they are always tempted. <br /> <br /> The paranoia, people's eyes linger on them too long. Potential blackmail, does somebody know? <br /> <br /> Did the prince say he was calling a blood hunt only to turn around after the fact and say it was never made public? Now he has you on a leash. <br /> <br /> You can build way more interesting narratives with it being hidden after a time. <br /> <br /> The friendly new kindred moved into town and has been very helpful. He has been paling around with one of the coterie. Now another kindred that moved to town a few years ago claims he was a suspect for a string of diableries. Is your coterie mate in danger. And when was the last time you saw them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:13:09-07:00","id":973052,"title":"","content":"Rape is outside my comfort zone. I distinguish between killing and murder. I think &quot;are you a diablerist&quot; and &quot;have you ever committed diablerie&quot; are practically the same question. It seems to me some people like to play dark superhero and Auspex 2 to find out if a person is a murderer or rapist would fit that well. The power does say it finds out secrets. If you prey on unsavory folk then you should have little trouble finding them. I can understand saying a vampire that last committed a murder a 100 years ago wouldn't register with Auspex 2 though.<br /> <br /> I view Auspex 2 as the power to use to find out enough info about a person to figure out what kind of person they are, their nature. You need Auspex 4 to dig deeper into the mind. If something is a breaking point for Integrity or Humanity then I think it should tend to be available for a query at Auspex 2. I view this not about the act but how it affects the individual. I also view breaking points for Integrity analogues, not necessarily all replacements, as trauma so I think a person learns to live with it rather than gets over it. Probably not a view for everyone.<br /> <br /> Vampires have paranoia as a defining characteristic. Mekhet are avoided because they have Auspex. What happens to those that are caught using Auspex regularly? Given that many a vampire would take precautions against other vampires so that a diablerist would not be seen as much of a personal threat, would vampires tend to view a diablerist or a nosy vampire that likes to use Auspex and tell everyone about all the juicy secrets found as the greater threat? I know the politically correct answer. Now how many vampires would act on their true feelings, I wonder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T05:56:30-07:00","id":973066,"title":"","content":"So, I think this prompts a bit of a question. Can Auspex 2 pick up anything in the past, so long as it counts as a &quot;weakness&quot; to be exploited? I personally think that's treading far too close to Auspex 3 and 4's ability to see into person's past / memories. All of the examples of Auspex 2 are about current secrets and flaws, something currently active, not buried memories. I'm going to personally argue that it has to be a secret that's currently affecting a person at the given moment. To me, the main purpose of Auspex 4 is to go delving into someone's memories for secrets from their past to pull out and use as blackmail. Control a person through their past deeds. I don't think that Auspex 2 is meant to overlap that much. <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The point (of Tainted) isn't to mark a Diablerist.&quot;<br /> Can't it be more than one thing? Why not serve a double purpose of both marking and inflicting problems? Two birds with one stone, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T08:02:34-07:00","id":973143,"title":"","content":"Auspex 2 lets you know they're a Diablerist. Auspex 4 lets you know how they did it, who they did it to, and make them feel guilty or scared over it. It also lets you know if they did it more than once.<br /> <br /> Relying on the Tainted Condition seems rough. A Vampire can burn the Tainted Condition out of themselves immediately after committing the act. If they only Diablerized a Blood Potency 1 Neonate, they only take a single point of damage, and the wound or scar (remember that aggravated damage causes scars for Vampires) can be hidden somewhere out of sight or explained some other way. It's just a matter of how much they're willing to hurt themselves to hide.<br /> <br /> Asking if someone is a Diablerist and having it read as &quot;No&quot; when they did it earlier that same night seems like actively working against the point of the ability and kind of being a dick to Mekhet characters. It's their whole schtick, to know secrets.<br /> <br /> Even if it's a Blood Potency 10 Ancient, the Tainted Condition doesn't even last a year.<br /> <br /> When the mind control power can control minds without spending Vitae at the first dot, and the Social power can make you loved even as you beat someone's face in at the same, and the hiding power makes you impossible to notice so long as other people are around... it seems arbitrary to make the secret-gathering power be unable to gather secrets that happened so recently on the time scale of immortals.<br /> <br /> Everyone is free to run their game how they like, but I think the &quot;only detect it when recent&quot; interpretation really goes against the grain both mechanically and thematically, and &quot;only detect it when Tainted&quot; is even worse for the reasons above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:25:44-07:00","id":973173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=972962#post972962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure this question would be legit with Auspex. I mean, if it would so you could also ask: &quot;Has this person killed/rape/rapt?&quot; But you can't ask for this kind of question (more suitable for Auspex 4), according to my interpretation at least.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Semantics, but important ones none the less. If &quot;Is this person a diablerist&quot; is a valid question, ( and listed in the book), I am not sure why you would think &quot;Have they commit diablerie?&quot; is not a valid question. They are so closely related that in most cases the answer would be the same. Only special cases would the answer be different. One is that you currently ARE and the other is you WERE at one point.<br /> <br /> I would give the answer based on the question asked. I let my players know how they word things should be important. I also let my players know I dont actively try to screw them so should they ask &quot;Is this person a diablerist?&quot; I would say, &quot; Do you mean currently or have they been?&quot; I try to figure out what my players mean before I answer the question.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I dont know what prince in their right mind would force a vampire to commit diablerie as punishment for a crime. It is really really addictive, plus the vitae addiction, and vampires who are addicted to doing it are extremely dangerous. You have to make a roll to NOT do it anytime you are faced with a chance to do it... and a chance to do it would be pretty much anytime you are alone in a room with a vampire. It's like Pringles, once you pop, you just cant stop...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 09-20-2016, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:35:42-07:00","id":973223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973066#post973066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I think this prompts a bit of a question. Can Auspex 2 pick up anything in the past, so long as it counts as a &amp;quot;weakness&amp;quot; to be exploited? I personally think that's treading far too close to Auspex 3 and 4's ability to see into person's past / memories. All of the examples of Auspex 2 are about current secrets and flaws, something currently active, not buried memories. I'm going to personally argue that it has to be a secret that's currently affecting a person at the given moment. To me, the main purpose of Auspex 4 is to go delving into someone's memories for secrets from their past to pull out and use as blackmail. Control a person through their past deeds. I don't think that Auspex 2 is meant to overlap that much. </div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, it's been nagging at me that I couldn't articulate why the ever a diablerist interpretation didn't feel right dispite it being the rules as wrighten answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:31:19-07:00","id":973255,"title":"","content":"I feel like the confusion here is mostly due to the changes in presentation of Auspex in 2e. In 1e, Auspex 2 was called &quot;Aura Perception&quot;, and it let you see an actual psychic halo of colors around someone, and through those colors you could discern all kinds of information like what their mood was, if they had any Derangements, the influence of possessing entities, if the person was a supernatural creature and what kind, etc., and yes, if they were a Diablerist. Theoretically, if everyone actually memorized the stupid color meanings chart, the ST could just describe the colors seen in someone's aura and the player would know what that meant. In practice, it usually ended up working by the player asking questions and the ST answering them, or at least that's how it worked in the games I played in. Either way, no one really questioned that even if you only commit Diablerie one time, 100 years ago, you would still read as a Diablerist to an Auspex 2 user, because it was described as black streaks in your aura that would be visible to anyone who could view your aura.<br /> <br /> 10+ years later, 2e decides to make a cosmetic change to the whole Aura thing. Vampires viewing colored halos around their victims and reading psychic impressions off of objects they touch isn't considered thematically appropriate any more, so the &quot;predatory aura&quot; becomes less of a psychic halo and more of a convenient way to describe all the subtle little tells vampires have and can recognize each other by - the way they move, the way they look at humans, the pallor of their skin, the forced way their chests rise and fall. Predator's Taint becomes Lashing Out, not an automatic clash of auras but conscious and overt displays of aggression, seduction, or dominance. Auspex 2 gets cleaned up to work the way many groups had been running it anyway, and gets re-named to &quot;Uncanny Perception&quot;. Instead of a new-age psychic reading, it's Lie To Me style observation of those subtle tells like microexpressions and nonverbal social cues (filtered through the perception of the Beast, of course). Now, because there's no actual halo of energy for Diablerie to stain, it's more of a strain on verisimilitude for some people that Diablerie would permanently change the Diablerist in such a way that would for ever be observable under this new, less psychic, more sensual version of Auspex 2.<br /> <br /> I suspect the intent was for the question &quot;is this person a Diablerist?&quot; to come up &quot;yes&quot; even if they had only done it once, 100 years ago (or if they are being possessed by a Strix). But I don't think tying it to something more conditional, like having Tainted or having Diablerie addiction is an unreasonable call to make. Ultimately it comes down to what you think will make for better game play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-20-2016, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:41:15-07:00","id":973258,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean. It's still psychic, no? Just you get hallucinations of a different sort than auras, given to you by your Beast.<br /> <br /> It's called <i>Uncanny Perception</i> but it's all bloody daggers and the smell of brimstone and the sound of barking dogs.<br /> <br /> Not that it particularly matters either way, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:06:55-07:00","id":973281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973258#post973258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean. It's still psychic, no? Just you get hallucinations of a different sort than auras, given to you by your Beast.<br /> <br /> It's called <i>Uncanny Perception</i> but it's all bloody daggers and the smell of brimstone and the sound of barking dogs.<br /> <br /> Not that it particularly matters either way, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. That was what I meant to suggest with the &quot;filtered through the perception of the Beast&quot; part. Now, this is just my personal interpretation, but I always figured the Beast interprets mundane sensory information like microexpressions that the vampire might not be keen enough to pick up on on her own, along with some extrasensory information that the vampire might not be able to percieve with sight, smell, hearing, and touch alone, and reports that information to the vampire in the form of what amounts to hallucinations.<br /> <br /> Either way, I think the change in the way it's presented, fom seeing aura colors to symbolic immagry is part of what is leading people to take issues with the idea of a single act of Diablerie permanently marking the Diablerist as such to Auspex users, when that issue was not taken with the previous incarnation of the power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:46:52-07:00","id":973305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973173#post973173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Semantics, but important ones none the less. If &quot;Is this person a diablerist&quot; is a valid question, ( and listed in the book), I am not sure why you would think &quot;Have they commit diablerie?&quot; is not a valid question. They are so closely related that in most cases the answer would be the same. Only special cases would the answer be different. One is that you currently ARE and the other is you WERE at one point.<br /> <br /> I would give the answer based on the question asked. I let my players know how they word things should be important. I also let my players know I dont actively try to screw them so should they ask &quot;Is this person a diablerist?&quot; I would say, &quot; Do you mean currently or have they been?&quot; I try to figure out what my players mean before I answer the question.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I dont know what prince in their right mind would force a vampire to commit diablerie as punishment for a crime. It is really really addictive, plus the vitae addiction, and vampires who are addicted to doing it are extremely dangerous. You have to make a roll to NOT do it anytime you are faced with a chance to do it... and a chance to do it would be pretty much anytime you are alone in a room with a vampire. It's like Pringles, once you pop, you just cant stop...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue &quot;*is* someone a something&quot;? Is a valid use of current information. Is someone who has stolen something a theft? Yes. Is someone who has murdered a murderer? Yes. Is someone who has committed diablerie a diablerist? Again, yes. It provides no context but does provide information which is a current and accurate label because it is about having passed through a threshold which once passed through puts a person permanently in a category. Because it doesn't ask about the subjects belief or memory, and answers the question independent of what the subject 'knows', it doesn't tread on the more powerful levels which are all about context and about the past/memories. Really if you think about it, the past is all about giving the present context.<br /> <br /> As a storyteller I would remind the players to keep their question present-tense to be a valid question. That's the main problem I see with &quot;Have they commit diablerie?&quot;<br /> <br /> Also about your edit: My thoughts would be this would be a common vampire reaction &quot;If the Prince condones Diablerie, it is time for a new prince, or to move from this Domain because I don't want to live where the Prince is a psychotic idiot and there are also diablerie addicts running around because of the aforementioned idiocy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also Auspex as evidence is extremely weak for publicly condemning others without either enough social clout to be able to condemn people falsely without material confirmation (applicable to Auspex users conspiring or sole individual's testimony), or actual evidence that can be confirmed outside of that power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-20-2016, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:04:26-07:00","id":973328,"title":"","content":"Diablerie didn't permanently taint the aura of its perpetrators in 1st edition. Only for the duration outlined in the description. Furthermore there was room for plausible deniability between penalties to detect it, resistance, and existing powers to conceal it. <br /> <br /> Now Auspex 2 is infallible and omniscient. Just be sure you play Jeopardy and phrase the information you want in the form of a question. Why should anyone have a problem with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-20-2016, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:58:08-07:00","id":973371,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/235363-diablerie-a-permanent-sin\">Seems like this isn't a new conversation. </a>And it seems like some of the same people were involved. Linking for convenience of reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-20-2016, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:04:26-07:00","id":973416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973328#post973328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diablerie didn't permanently taint the aura of its perpetrators in 1st edition. Only for the duration outlined in the description. Furthermore there was room for plausible deniability between penalties to detect it, resistance, and existing powers to conceal it.<br /> <br /> Now Auspex 2 is infallible and omniscient. Just be sure you play Jeopardy and phrase the information you want in the form of a question. Why should anyone have a problem with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Infallible omniscience isn't particularly useful if it's completely unverifiable, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:13:00-07:00","id":973420,"title":"","content":"Okay so an earlier post by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> cleared up where I was going wrong, so yeah - tainted condition has nothing to do with how long you can be identified as a diablerist, and Auspex 2 does suggest there's no time limit on the questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:14:12-07:00","id":973422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973281#post973281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much. That was what I meant to suggest with the &amp;quot;filtered through the perception of the Beast&amp;quot; part. Now, this is just my personal interpretation, but I always figured the Beast interprets mundane sensory information like microexpressions that the vampire might not be keen enough to pick up on on her own, along with some extrasensory information that the vampire might not be able to percieve with sight, smell, hearing, and touch alone, and reports that information to the vampire in the form of what amounts to hallucinations.<br /> <br /> Either way, I think the change in the way it's presented, fom seeing aura colors to symbolic immagry is part of what is leading people to take issues with the idea of a single act of Diablerie permanently marking the Diablerist as such to Auspex users, when that issue was not taken with the previous incarnation of the power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your point of view but, what about touch of spirit? Objects don't have microexpression but they still provide hallucinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:21:11-07:00","id":973429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973422#post973422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point of view but, what about touch of spirit? Objects don't have microexpression but they still provide hallucinations.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where it starts getting into extrasensory perseption. The Beast has a sort of 6th sense that the vampire doesn't have. I guess you could make the point that's pretty much the definition of psychic, and I wouldn't argue with that. I mean, heck, Lay Open the Mind is outright telepathy. But I think the progression in 2e works in its favor - going from danger sense, to preternatural psychoanalysis, to sensing impressions from objects, to telepathy, to remote sensing just feels better than going from enhanced senses right into aura reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:25:13-07:00","id":973476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973416#post973416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infallible omniscience isn't particularly useful if it's completely unverifiable, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that it IS totally verifiable. That's the part that gets me. All you need is one Sheriff with one of those powers or abilities, and tada. Verification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:42:12-07:00","id":973486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973416#post973416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infallible omniscience isn't particularly useful if it's completely unverifiable, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually omniscience is extremely useful because unless you're Cassandra, infallible omniscience is useful for building credibility. It's just not very useful for making yourself popular by trying to lord it over someone who's more well liked than you are. (Which is typically the case when you're talking about nosy snitches.)<br /> And it's usefulness or lack thereof has nothing to do with its inherent obnoxiousness when there are no limits or restrictions placed on its use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973476#post973476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except that it IS totally verifiable. That's the part that gets me. All you need is one Sheriff with one of those powers or abilities, and tada. Verification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or someone with Veridical Tongue or Liar's Plague in their repertoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-20-2016, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:47:31-07:00","id":973488,"title":"","content":"I don't really care how long it takes. If the tainted condition being the determining factor is an issue for some that's fine. Perhaps 1 year per dot of blood potency. Whatever..<br /> <br /> It's the fact that as a storyteller you can never sneak a horrible monster into a particularly paranoid group by asking 1 question....<br /> <br /> Sure with enough digging and some clever uses of auspex they may figure it out anyway. But 1 question ruining a plot is awful.<br /> <br /> That's just bad for anyone wanting to add some serious horror into their game. <br /> <br /> I would personally kick out any raw rule that made this the case.<br /> <br /> And as for players, diablerie is a great tool for all kinds of fun for the ST and the player to get up shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T17:37:00-07:00","id":973523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973488#post973488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really care how long it takes. If the tainted condition being the determining factor is an issue for some that's fine. Perhaps 1 year per dot of blood potency. Whatever..<br /> <br /> It's the fact that as a storyteller you can never sneak a horrible monster into a particularly paranoid group by asking 1 question....<br /> <br /> Sure with enough digging and some clever uses of auspex they may figure it out anyway. But 1 question ruining a plot is awful.<br /> <br /> That's just bad for anyone wanting to add some serious horror into their game.<br /> <br /> I would personally kick out any raw rule that made this the case.<br /> <br /> And as for players, diablerie is a great tool for all kinds of fun for the ST and the player to get up shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or... Make a devotion that hides the fact that you regularly eat souls. That would be even more scary. Not that The Unholy even bothered with such measures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T18:47:33-07:00","id":973570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973476#post973476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except that it IS totally verifiable. That's the part that gets me. All you need is one Sheriff with one of those powers or abilities, and tada. Verification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, this hypothetical city is putting a <i>lot</i> of power in the hands of its Sheriff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:01:51-07:00","id":973579,"title":"","content":"Especially considering the sheriff operates in a city where someone can simply put the thought that 'x has commit diablerie' in their head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:27:32-07:00","id":973592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973570#post973570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, this hypothetical city is putting a <i>lot</i> of power in the hands of its Sheriff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh isn't it kinda his job to hunt down things like this and bring them to the prince for judgement?<br /> <br /> This isn't hypothetical. It's just kinda normally how it works right?<br /> <br /> Doesn't matter if he has auspex. It would be up to the prince to decide. But if he could back up the claim it would make for a fast trial I'd imagine. <br /> <br /> Also, a sheriff that was easy to dominate likely wouldn't remain sheriff for long, or would at the very least use all his authority to bring that person to the prince for judgement. I would imagine most princes would take that as a direct assault on their authority.<br /> <br /> So yeah perfectly reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:34:55-07:00","id":973595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973592#post973592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh isn't it kinda his job to hunt down things like this and bring them to the prince for judgement?<br /> <br /> This isn't hypothetical. It's just kinda normally how it works right?</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's someone killing vampires, sure. Using Auspex on random vampires to find out their secrets would lead to a short career.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, a sheriff that was easy to dominate likely wouldn't remain sheriff for long, or would at the very least use all his authority to bring that person to the prince for judgement. I would imagine most princes would take that as a direct assault on their authority.<br /> <br /> So yeah perfectly reasonable. </div> </div> </div>Or a sheriff that was easy to Dominate is an excellent one. No Prince wants someone out there gathering secrets on everyone and not being under their control.<br /> <br /> But even if you weren't 'easy' to Dominate, that just means the one who did it was powerful.<br /> <br /> Auspex is fallible. And too many executions based on that fallibility would lead to unrest.<br /> <br /> Like basically everything in the game, all the Chronicles games, it's going to depend. No one can do anything about the Nameless ganking whoever they want. If the domain is a tyrant's paradise, then the Prince can get away with letting their sheriffs do whatever they want. In a more balanced domain, it's going to lead to chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-20-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:42:58-07:00","id":973597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973595#post973595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there's someone killing vampires, sure. Using Auspex on random vampires to find out their secrets would lead to a short career.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or a sheriff that was easy to Dominate is an excellent one. No Prince wants someone out there gathering secrets on everyone and not being under their control.<br /> <br /> But even if you weren't 'easy' to Dominate, that just means the one who did it was powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original argument was that a person goes to the sheriff and tells him &quot;Person X is a diabolist&quot; then the sheriff would be required to check into it. If he had auspex it is totally in his right to use that tool or any others he possesses to verify. If he believes it's true it's his job to bring them in for the prince to decide. <br /> <br /> He's not sifting through all their secrets. But if &quot;Is this person a diabolist&quot; is on the table, it's a perfectly valid thing for him to inspect whoever he wants. It's not him digging through everybody's secrets. That's him finding a murderer in the city. <br /> <br /> Also, no a sheriff that is easy to dominate would be a good sheriff by any princes standards. Someone could learn all his secrets or even turn the sheriff on him. Any prince that selected a weak sheriff likely won't remain prince for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:47:09-07:00","id":973599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973592#post973592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh isn't it kinda his job to hunt down things like this and bring them to the prince for judgement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but any court worth its salt is going to require evidence before they just take it on the Sheriff's word that someone is a Diablerist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973592#post973592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't hypothetical. It's just kinda normally how it works right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It normally works that anyone who claims to have used Auspex to find out that someone is a Diablerist and paid off the Sheriff can condemn anyone they want to to Final Death? Not in my games. Auspex cannot be corroborated by any means besides the say-so of other Auspex users. Heck, the <i>fact that someone has Auspex</i> can't even be corroborated very easily. It should absolutely not be admissible evidence in any self-respecting court.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973592#post973592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't matter if he has auspex. It would be up to the prince to decide. But if he could back up the claim it would make for a fast trial I'd imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he could back up the claim then that's a totally different story. What I'm getting at is, Auspex may be pretty foolproof in detecting Diablerists, but it doesn't do anything to actually prove Diablerie to anyone but the Auspex user herself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973592#post973592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a sheriff that was easy to dominate likely wouldn't remain sheriff for long, or would at the very least use all his authority to bring that person to the prince for judgement. I would imagine most princes would take that as a direct assault on their authority.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said anything about Dominate. Like I said earlier in the thread, giving self-proclaimed Auspex users the power to condemn any member of your court as a Diablerist without any supporting evidence aside from agreement from other self-proclaimed Auspex users is a great way to get yourself in a Salem witch trial situation. And a smart Prince should know better.<br /> <br /> Auspex is a good starting point for an investigation, but it shouldn't be enough to get people to actually <i>believe</i> your assertions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T19:55:50-07:00","id":973601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>overload</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973597#post973597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original argument was that a person goes to the sheriff and tells him &quot;Person X is a diabolist&quot; then the sheriff would be required to check into it. If he had auspex it is totally in his right to use that tool or any others he possesses to verify. If he believes it's true it's his job to bring them in for the prince to decide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you point me to that original argument? I looked but cannot find that. Just Charlaquin pointing out that Auspex was not verifiable, then MCN said having one sheriff with Auspex means it's verified.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it depends on the laws and beliefs of the domain. There's a bloodline that forever taints the members with the marks of diablerie, this might mean something if anyone in the domain knows about them, or is one. There's revenants who were base animals before committing diablerie and becoming 'true' vampires. There's vampires that have lived thousands of years, including through times when diablerie was acceptable. And sometimes a person is too valuable or too important to do anything to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He's not sifting through all their secrets. But if &quot;Is this person a diabolist&quot; is on the table, it's a perfectly valid thing for him to inspect whoever he wants. It's not him digging through everybody's secrets. That's him finding a murderer in the city. </div> </div> </div>Except it isn't. The diablerie could have been committed elsewhere. Or they could simply claim the diablerie was committed elsewhere. If they're a serial diabolist, it's entirely possible that would ping as true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, no a sheriff that is easy to dominate would be a good sheriff by any princes standards. Someone could learn all his secrets or even turn the sheriff on him. Any prince that selected a weak sheriff likely won't remain prince for long. </div> </div> </div>The sheriff just investigates and enforces the law, the Prince should have a lot more protecting them. The Hound, for instance, is traditionally more loyal to the Prince than the sheriff is. And that's just with a more traditional Princedom. There's many different kinds of setups, without Princes or sheriffs.<br /> <br /> But anyways, having a weak-minded sheriff is the type of ploy a Prince would pull if they wanted to make a gesture about caring about vampire law and order and not really giving a damn about it. It's entirely possible the Prince is a diabolist anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-20-2016, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:55:02-07:00","id":973758,"title":"","content":"I've already given my position earlier which is that having a &quot;I know you're guilty&quot; button is a significant constrainer on a GM's plots. And that attempts I've seen to get around it become increasingly circumstantial and convoluted. So I removed the button. And that's pretty much the sum total of my position on this to be taken or left by other GMs as they wish. However, I'm still reading this thread out of interest and I feel like I have to weigh in to defend overload's position here.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Prince doesn't regard the lowly PCs as trustworthy enough to take their word that someone is a diablerist. Maybe the Sheriff doesn't have the power or influence to act on their own use of Auspex because it isn't proof. These are all valid circumstances in which the ability to detect in a foolproof way that someone is a diablerist isn't a show stopper to a plot or character concept. And they could be true of any given GM's campaign. But the question of whether being able to detect diablerie is a big constraint on games doesn't depend on whether there are cases where it isn't; it depends on whether there's a wide range of circumstances where it is. And I'd pretty confidently argue that there are.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head for general ideas:<ul><li>The PC group is trying to decide whether to trust friendly new NPC. It doesn't matter whether they can convince the prince of something or not, you've immediately ruled out any given NPC hiding their nefarious deeds from the player group and for a very wide range of plots, that's all that matters. They might not be able to secure a conviction but goodbye to pulling the wool over the PC's eyes.</li> <li>The powerful and influential prince is a staple of Vampire games. Such a figure may be absolutely fine taking their own word for it and not having to prove it in a court of law to their lessers. So you lose out on plots any plots that combine such a prince with another vampire being a diablarist.</li> <li>The Prince scenario pretty much holds true for any other elder who is in a position of power over the diablerist. If Diablerie is this heinous crime, then it doesn't matter so much if the prince / sheriff / powerful elder can prove it - they personally know it for a fact and will act accordingly. In vampire society, a court of law is not typically the thing a vampire most fears - a powerful enemy knowing you're a diablerist will be sufficient. Rumour, personal influence, two or three Auspex users agreeing and backing each other up. All is sufficient to bring down a diablerist.</li> </ul><br /> I could come up with plenty more. Having an &quot;I know you're guilty&quot; button is very constraining on a GM or even a player. It cuts out a tonne of character options unless Auspex 2 is uncharacteristically rare. Certainly for all of the above you can twist and turn and find ways around it, but I want to be able to just stick in a character without or campaign event without having to twist around all sorts of things to justify someone not being outed, exiled, hunted, socially excluded / whatever because it's easy to see that they're really a terrible person.<br /> <br /> That's my view on it. It's bad because it is constrains the campaign a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:12:25-07:00","id":973765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973570#post973570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, this hypothetical city is putting a <i>lot</i> of power in the hands of its Sheriff.</div> </div> </div> </div> Man, this hypothetical city is using a standard model for a city, as described in Damnation City. Its almost like people are used to the idea of the tyrant Prince and her faithful Sheriff / judge-jury-executioner as a common thing in many games. Its almost like someone actually -plays- in this hypothetical city, which might happen to be set in LA and some rather detailed and powerful NPC figures. <br /> <br /> Its also possible that this hypothetical city has a mass of vampires that can individually confirm or deny these charges, practically at whim, through a variety of Disciplines and blood magics, making such accusations a chorus instead of a lone voice. Or, rather, discovering if the accuser is a bad liar and openly mocking the accuser. Harpies would eat that shit up.<br /> <br /> Its further possible that we'd have vigilantee action, especialy from the Lancea et Sanctum or Invictus knighthoods. Maybe the city has formalized Laws that require investigations and trials, where the word of appointed specialists hold weight in court; take a look at Requiem for Rome - the word of a formal divination held a LOT of weight. Yes, the diviners could be bribed, but the point is that the word of seers holding lots of influence over vampire judgements is well established in the game, contrary to what you are suggesting. Perhaps this is an Acolyte or Dragon domain where its an anarchy rule of the strong, and cotories seek out accused diablerists out of self preservation; most cotories do trust the words of their mates.<br /> <br /> I could go on. There's a million ways that this could play out when you have reliable methods of detecting diablerie easily. You may run your game in a way that makes it easy for a diablerist to slip through the cracks, but there's just as many people, if not more, who run games in a way where your method makes absolutely no sense. Certainly, I can't see how such accusations can easily be brushed off when over half of a city's vampire population can independantly verify this practically at whim, including authority figures. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to be honest, Charlaquin. This &quot;hypothetical&quot; city of yours where the Sheriff has no power to investigate such a rumor, where vampires courts rely on physical evidence and won't accept blood sorcery or trusted Auspex users or make judgements by popular opinion makes zero sense for the &quot;hypothetical&quot; city I actually use. Seriously, don't be dismissive of someone and call their actual play experience as &quot;hypothetical.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:48:19-07:00","id":973777,"title":"","content":"Pretty much summed up the points I was trying to make, just more eloquently Knasser and MCN.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of what if and hypothetical situations we could go through. My point is, having a big red shiny binary answer button is not a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:12:12-07:00","id":973791,"title":"","content":"Uh. Okay. So.<br /> <br /> 1. If a Vampire in a position of power doesn't care what other people think and are going to persecute whoever they want without giving a damn about evidence or swaying others to their cause, then the Domain has far more serious problems than Auspex and is going to be toppled soon regardless. Auspex isn't going to tip the scales in that regard. It doesn't matter if they have Auspex or not, acting like that is going to have every Vampire in the domain wondering if it'll be them next. And they'd be right to wonder.<br /> <br /> 2. Even if they do have Auspex and know someone is guilty, as we've been saying, nobody else knows. Even if they believe the vampire with Auspex this time, and that belief was right, who's to say that the vampire with Auspex won't take advantage of this? Sure, today they point out a Diablerist. Tomorrow, it's their centuries-old Rival who they claim is a Diablerist. He isn't, of course, but this is what happens when you believe an Auspex user on their word and their word alone. Maybe we've been focusing too much on the &quot;it can't be verified&quot; angle because that's only half the problem. The other problem is <i>Vampires lie</i>. Trusting an Auspex user today means he can accuse you tomorrow of something you never did.<br /> <br /> 3. For the &quot;but you can't hide it from players!&quot; argument... why can't you? If you're okay with homebrewing content, have them use a Devotion or Sorcery to mask it. If you aren't, you could have them not be a diablerist -yet-. Either way, do your players just randomly Auspex everyone they meet with the Diablerist question? If so you have problems with your group beyond the scope of this thread. (Edit: Because of Diablerie in specific, not Auspex. Auspex is kind of intended to be used frequently. Diablerie is just oddly specific and makes me think metagaming is occuring) That's like Googling everyone you meet the moment you meet them.<br /> <br /> The way I see this? One option is hindering players by taking something away from their established niche (making the Secret Gathering power arbitrarily unable to gather some secrets). The other option is encourages stories by providing obstacles to overcome and doesn't take anything away from anyone except the ability to commit a perfect crime, and perfect crimes only shut stories down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":".  Edit: Clarifying #3 for @Holy 09-21-2016, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:12:44-07:00","id":973792,"title":"","content":"Or you could be a less predictable ST with your NPCs.<br /> <br /> Have the vampire that committed Diablerie years ago be the one vampire that is truly wishing to help them out. Make a story about it. \u201cDon\u00b4t look at me that way, you weren\u00b4t here on the days preceding the Birth of the Blood God, I did what I had to do survive the Circle\u00b4s predation and ensure that the Movement would endure.\u201d<br /> <br /> Have the squeaky clean benefactor be a true monster just starting on the downward spiral. Guess who he plans to be his first victims? \u201cOf course I have a safe place for you and your coterie to hide from that unjust sheriff! But I have to smuggle you in, so get inside these reinforced steel boxes so I can take you there! Don\u00b4t even worry about feeding, I have blood dolls galore! Hehehehe!\u201d<br /> <br /> Once the players understand that one answer to one question can't* unravel your plots you won\u00b4t have this problem.<br /> <br /> So don\u00b4t let your plots be unraveled by one question and answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":".  *can't not can 09-21-2016, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:37:16-07:00","id":973812,"title":"","content":"Vampires are often described as paranoid and power-hungry. Using Auspex regularly would fuel both of those tropes. So, not sure I agree with Maina that PCs using it regularly means your group has a problem. If they're just talking about power-spamming as a meta-concept, that could be a different argument, but considering other disciplines have free always-on abilities, I'm less convinced.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of diablerie as a common concept - seen it abused in too many group games - so I tend to be sympathetic to the idea that it is always something that's detectable. In 2E, though - there have been a lot of ways to make Auspex more powerful:<ul><li>No base cost.</li> <li>No inherent resistance for the victim</li> <li>No more penalties for time (It was harder to learn old secrets in 1E)</li> <li>Obfuscate can no longer hide your Aura, forcing a Clash of Wills like 1E did.</li> </ul>That means it is far, far easier to detect a diablerist (however you define that). I would hazard that 75% of Mekhet PCs I've encountered through all games I've been in have started out with Auspex 2. NPCs will fall lower than that, but still. When something's that easy, I agree with MCN - you have to get pretty convoluted in your power structure to write off that chorus.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think 2E has skewed a little too far in Auspex's favor, but that's personal preference.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to fix it (not sure I do), I might consider a couple routes:<ul><li>Uncanny Perception only reveals secrets from the past X. (X probably would be 1 year. Telepathy would let you dig for older memories, but can be countered by Dominate.)</li> <li>Modify the &quot;Are they a diablerist?&quot; question to, &quot;Are they a diablerist, like me?&quot; (Takes one to know one. Now there's a weird political/effectiveness reason to NOT just destroy all Amaranthines automatically and becomes a cold war of sorts in the accusation realm.)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":".  spelling 09-21-2016, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:50:22-07:00","id":973848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973792#post973792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could be a less predictable ST with your NPCs.<br /> <br /> Have the vampire that committed Diablerie years ago be the one vampire that is truly wishing to help them out. Make a story about it. \u201cDon\u00b4t look at me that way, you weren\u00b4t here on the days preceding the Birth of the Blood God, I did what I had to do survive the Circle\u00b4s predation and ensure that the Movement would endure.\u201d<br /> <br /> Have the squeaky clean benefactor be a true monster just starting on the downward spiral. Guess who he plans to be his first victims? \u201cOf course I have a safe place for you and your coterie to hide from that unjust sheriff! But I have to smuggle you in, so get inside these reinforced steel boxes so I can take you there!</div> </div> </div> </div>This falls under either a convoluted exception that an ST has to pull out of their ass or simply design chronicles where diablerie is normal and acceptable. Neither character suggestion you offered would survive an initial encounter with my group. The first one would be outed and destroyed or avoided whenever possible as a diablerist. No chance to offer excuses. And the second character even if he had never committed diablerie, a question to the effect of &quot;what is this character's ulterior motive regarding me or what does he expect from me in payment?&quot; would be immediately demanded. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So don\u00b4t let your plots be unraveled by one question and answer. </div> </div> </div>It's not one question that unravels the plot. It's the fact that they get to ask an infinite number of questions about anything and so long as the answer isn't universal or common knowledge, the question is &quot;perfectly valid&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:19:33-07:00","id":973865,"title":"","content":"They can't ask infinite questions. Questions after the first require Vitae.<br /> <br /> I'm having trouble understanding this position in particular.<br /> <br /> What makes &quot;the ability to find secrets&quot; so much worse than invisibility, mind control, forcing everyone in the room to like you no matter what you do, superhuman strength, moving faster than the eye can register, etc, etc, etc? A starting character can have any of those without minmaxing or any bad faith decisions. Hell, every Vampire character starts with at least one way to &quot;break&quot; a story with a single use of their abilities.<br /> <br /> It's not &quot;convoluted exceptions.&quot; It's a basic fact of Vampire storytelling; if you don't take into account your group's abilities, they can (and maybe will) break your story.<br /> <br /> What, to you, makes Auspex special in this regard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:37:02-07:00","id":973873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973848#post973848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...an ST has to pull out of their ass...</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's turn this into Jeopardy;<br /> <br /> What is something an ST pulls out of their ass?<br /> <br /> The whole goddamn story!<br /> <br /> Now that this is out of the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973848#post973848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or simply design chronicles where diablerie is normal and acceptable. Neither character suggestion you offered would survive an initial encounter with my group. The first one would be outed and destroyed or avoided whenever possible as a diablerist. No chance to offer excuses. And the second character even if he had never committed diablerie, a question to the effect of &quot;what is this character's ulterior motive regarding me or what does he expect from me in payment?&quot; would be immediately demanded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u00b4m not really following your argument. You assume the players have the power and political mandate to destroy the Diablerist who may be able to destroy them instead or be someone dear to the vampiric community who will have their asses for killing him. And hey, if they are able to and want to destroy the only person willing to help them, let them commit self-righteous suicide (trust in my).<br /> <br /> You can\u00b4t ask any question. It has to be about weakness. The fact the guy offering you shelter is planning to eat you is not his weakness, <b>it's yours.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973848#post973848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not one question that unravels the plot. It's the fact that they get to ask an infinite number of questions about anything and so long as the answer isn't universal or common knowledge, the question is &quot;perfectly valid&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>As stated by many others. Subsequent questions are not free. Hunger, predation and paranoia are themes of the game. Do whatever you want for your table, but don\u00b4t argue that the mechanic is not usable because you don\u00b4t know how or don\u00b4t care to use it in your game. Just makes you look like a poor ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 09-21-2016, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:56:58-07:00","id":973879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973865#post973865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes &quot;the ability to find secrets&quot; so much worse than invisibility, mind control, forcing everyone in the room to like you no matter what you do, superhuman strength, moving faster than the eye can register, etc, etc, etc? A starting character can have any of those without minmaxing or any bad faith decisions. Hell, every Vampire character starts with at least one way to &quot;break&quot; a story with a single use of their abilities.<br /> <br /> It's not &quot;convoluted exceptions.&quot; It's a basic fact of Vampire storytelling; if you don't take into account your group's abilities, they can (and maybe will) break your story.<br /> <br /> What, to you, makes Auspex special in this regard?</div> </div> </div> </div>Invisibility, mind control, and the other things you pointed out are limited on time; really strong but, you use invisibility to escape/ambush some main png, you use main control on him and ok...A prepared ST can handle it. Mind control ends. The point with Auspex is that, if you do something, whenever you did it, you always can know. You can't hide you can't handle. If you meet the Auspex user (not so rare also for the official png) your secret will be discovered. This is my thought <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:01:16-07:00","id":973881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973476#post973476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Except that it IS totally verifiable. That's the part that gets me. All you need is one Sheriff with one of those powers or abilities, and tada. Verification.</div> </div> </div> </div>One <i>uncorrupt</i> Sheriff, in a vampire society... Sheriff who has interest in proving a young welp a liar and poof, (or a sheriff that obey/is influenced by someone so interested) it is no different than any witness without physical evidence.<br /> <br /> Given how the Danse Macabre is portrayed in cannon, entirely virtuous enforcement of law is very uncommon.<br /> <br /> It is unverifiable in the sense it is based on non-universal perceptions, meaning it comes down solely to testimony. Have someone in power willing to testify on your behalf would be great but assume just because they have the capacity they will without expecting something in return is naive in cannon Requiem.<br /> <br /> Lets compare it to real life forensic information, just because you have a lab to do the test doesn't mean people will believe you unbiased, nor would they take it as valid evidence if they assumed you had reasons to falsify the results. Might some do their own lab testing and then use that information as best interests them? Absolutely, but odds are people in authority have already done that, and would only resent someone spouting their mouth off to make them look like they didn't investigate, when it isn't the younger vampire's place to dictate &quot;truth&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-21-2016, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:23:18-07:00","id":973893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973881#post973881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets compare it to real life forensic information, just because you have a lab to do the test doesn't mean people will believe you unbiased, nor would they take it as valid evidence if they assumed you had reasons to lie. Might some do their own lab testing and then use that information as best interests them? Absolutely, but odds are people in authority have already done that, and would only resent someone spouting their mouth off to make them look like they didn't investigate, when it isn't the younger vampire's place to dictate &quot;truth&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except this doesn't hold when the majority of entry level scientists can tell just by showing up to court and looking at the evidence. And 1/5th of your population are scientists.<br /> <br /> This paranoia works great as a thematic. It breaks down in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> It's a great scene if the Sheriff rolls into Elysium - accuses someone of diablerie - the Mekhet all look and see the Sheriff is lying but not a single one speaks up. Great scene, but tricky to pull off in a live game. I've been in way too many pickup, convention and LARP games to believe otherwise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:51:26-07:00","id":973904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973893#post973893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except this doesn't hold when the majority of entry level scientists can tell just by showing up to court and looking at the evidence. And 1/5th of your population are scientists.<br /> <br /> This paranoia works great as a thematic. It breaks down in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> It's a great scene if the Sheriff rolls into Elysium - accuses someone of diablerie - the Mekhet all look and see the Sheriff is lying but not a single one speaks up. Great scene, but tricky to pull off in a live game. I've been in way too many pickup, convention and LARP games to believe otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is funny you say this, because that is exactly the kind of thing that happens in our games. I play with the same people for a very long time, so maybe our group just has a jaded and cynic opinion of vampires in general and even more so of their society.<br /> <br /> Irredeemable meddlers don\u00b4t last too long. Call out the wrong lie and you might get blasted with the poor sop anyways, and now it is the new &quot;truth&quot;. Doing the right thing is not always the right choice. Know the rules of the game, your hand and if possible your opponent\u00b4s before making your play. Being a bystander in the face of evil and wrongness in action is one of the first falls in slipping Humanity and personal horror. <br /> <br /> &quot;All that is necessary for evil to triumph is that good men do nothing&quot; and all that.<br /> <br /> How many of you correct your bosses when they are unjustly scolding a colleague to shift blame in front of a higher-up? How many would if that correcting could very well lead you to being a bloodless corpse next to other guy? How about if you have this sense that higher-ups don\u00b4t really care for the truth and just playing their part on the circus?<br /> <br /> Those are very basic assumptions in the stories we run, and a common ground as we pass around the ST mantle.<br /> <br /> Isn\u00b4t this the Danse Macabre? Seems that are too many paladins running around in some people\u00b4s Chronicles of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:57:46-07:00","id":973908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973765#post973765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Man, this hypothetical city is using a standard model for a city, as described in Damnation City. Its almost like people are used to the idea of the tyrant Prince and her faithful Sheriff / judge-jury-executioner as a common thing in many games. Its almost like someone actually -plays- in this hypothetical city, which might happen to be set in LA and some rather detailed and powerful NPC figures. <br /> <br /> Its also possible that this hypothetical city has a mass of vampires that can individually confirm or deny these charges, practically at whim, through a variety of Disciplines and blood magics, making such accusations a chorus instead of a lone voice. Or, rather, discovering if the accuser is a bad liar and openly mocking the accuser. Harpies would eat that shit up.<br /> <br /> Its further possible that we'd have vigilantee action, especialy from the Lancea et Sanctum or Invictus knighthoods. Maybe the city has formalized Laws that require investigations and trials, where the word of appointed specialists hold weight in court; take a look at Requiem for Rome - the word of a formal divination held a LOT of weight. Yes, the diviners could be bribed, but the point is that the word of seers holding lots of influence over vampire judgements is well established in the game, contrary to what you are suggesting. Perhaps this is an Acolyte or Dragon domain where its an anarchy rule of the strong, and cotories seek out accused diablerists out of self preservation; most cotories do trust the words of their mates.<br /> <br /> I could go on. There's a million ways that this could play out when you have reliable methods of detecting diablerie easily. You may run your game in a way that makes it easy for a diablerist to slip through the cracks, but there's just as many people, if not more, who run games in a way where your method makes absolutely no sense. Certainly, I can't see how such accusations can easily be brushed off when over half of a city's vampire population can independantly verify this practically at whim, including authority figures. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to be honest, Charlaquin. This &amp;quot;hypothetical&amp;quot; city of yours where the Sheriff has no power to investigate such a rumor, where vampires courts rely on physical evidence and won't accept blood sorcery or trusted Auspex users or make judgements by popular opinion makes zero sense for the &amp;quot;hypothetical&amp;quot; city I actually use. Seriously, don't be dismissive of someone and call their actual play experience as &amp;quot;hypothetical.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah. I'm sorry if my use of the word hypothetical upset you. I'm gonna step out now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:05:27-07:00","id":973912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973893#post973893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except this doesn't hold when the majority of entry level scientists can tell just by showing up to court and looking at the evidence. And 1/5th of your population are scientists.<br /> <br /> This paranoia works great as a thematic. It breaks down in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> It's a great scene if the Sheriff rolls into Elysium - accuses someone of diablerie - the Mekhet all look and see the Sheriff is lying but not a single one speaks up. Great scene, but tricky to pull off in a live game. I've been in way too many pickup, convention and LARP games to believe otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonderful counter argument! My anecdotal LARP experience supports your claim but I've always believed that had to do with the players not actually being vampire who've gone through an extreme hazing period to disabuse them of modern notions of democratic justice and the individual's right to speak up, nor coming from an age when that wasn't as acceptable and not digging deep enough to get into that mindset. ie people playing vampires as if they were people with powers instead of supernaturally damned trauma victims who've been systematically abused to accept the status quo for fear of further harm.<br /> <br /> I've viewed it as not providing the correct incentives to roleplay such an alien paradigm that cannon presents as normal for the setting. I do like the carrot and stick method that 2nd uses extensively, and to encourage such epic scenes as your example scene, I as a storyteller might offer extra beats for playing within setting norms (similar to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801807#post801807\">Applicable Experience </a>Hack I have in my Frailty Chronicles).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973904#post973904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is funny you say this, because that is exactly the kind of thing that happens in our games. I play with the same people for a very long time, so maybe our group just has a jaded and cynic opinion of vampires in general and even more so of their society.<br /> <br /> Irredeemable meddlers don\u00b4t last too long. Call out the wrong lie and you might get blasted with the poor sop anyways, and now it is the new &quot;truth&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is wonderful to see my anecdotal experience isn't universal, also congratulations on have attended some really great games. The tabletop games I run are likewise an intrigue heavy corrupt danse macabre culture as the backdrop and I ensure to induct the players into the themes, moods and in-game paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-21-2016, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:27:24-07:00","id":973920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973912#post973912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've viewed it as not providing the correct incentives to roleplay such an alien paradigm that cannon presents as normal for the setting. I do like the carrot and stick method that 2nd uses extensively, and to encourage such epic scenes as your example scene, I as a storyteller might offer extra beats for playing within setting norms (similar to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801807#post801807\">Applicable Experience </a>Hack I have in my Frailty Chronicles).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh. This is interesting, thank you for the link.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:54:14-07:00","id":973987,"title":"","content":"One day it will be possible to make a criticism of a game system without somebody responding that the critic just needs to &quot;be a better GM&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The corrollary to saying &quot;this isn't a problem if you're a better GM&quot; is to say &quot;if you're not, then you have a problem&quot;. I've never liked the &quot;You must be this high a GM to ride this game system&quot;. Not if it's a needless restriction. I think it's fair to say that my post was correct - it IS constraining to have an easily available &quot;I know you're guilty&quot; button in the game. That's undeniable because I list circumstances all day long that it constrains a GM or player from doing. &quot;I want my character to be a secret diablerist / sorry, it's not possible to keep diablerie secret&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm not even convinced you can put some simple ranking of better or worse on people because of their game tastes. Is it fair to say that a GM who wants a tyranical prince with Auspex is a &quot;worse&quot; GM than one that wants a city filled with laws, councils and judicial process? I don't think so. You can claim that one GM is putting more effort into inventive solutions to get around the constraints, but I don't think you can say they're &quot;a better GM&quot; just because the other wants a despotic ruler. Someone criticized the idea of a powerful prince not caring what others thought. Well that's what power is for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Anyway, I don't want to get too specific in my responses here because this conversation seems to be getting heated, so I'll summarize: if someone is saying that the solution to a constraint is being &quot;a better GM&quot; then they're acknowledging that it's a constraint. And lets be blunt - it's a big constraint. There's a terrible crime in vampire society and there's an easily accessible way to tell whether or not someone is guilty of it. That closes a lot of doors.<br /> <br /> Now I don't think anybody has said that this is a problem for everybody nor that it should be. But if it closes a lot of doors and creates a big problem for those of us who are not &quot;better GMs&quot;, then it is by definition constraining.<br /> <br /> And if it's constraining without some good stuff to offset that constraint, then I don't personally see it as a good bargain.<br /> <br /> Someone asked for a reason why this is bad but Invisibilty isn't. Let's answer that. Invisibility is far more easily worked around at a campaign level than detecting secrets like Diablerie. It throws up problems for a GM like &quot;just having someone stand guard wont be enough to stop them getting inside&quot; or &quot;they'll be able to follow someone home&quot;. The thing is, you're hard put to think of problems Invisibility throws up that can't also be achieved other ways. So invisibility lets you sneak into the party? So would forging invitations or scaling the walls or gas form... Invisibilty lets you walk right behind that elder on his way home to find out where their haven is? You could use a drone or a tracking device or a few mortals doing hand-off tailing. Invisibility throws up practical level scene challenges. And there are lots of ways of mitigating it that any GM can use. Making invisibillity engaging and a challenge is mostly just a question of resource - give them a dog, give them a fancy security system, etc.. And resource solutions are easy for a GM. Knowing someone's secrets is a campaign-level problem. It can't usually be solved with resource solutions, it has consequences way beyond adventure level abilities such as invisibility. And what do we get in return for these constraints? The difficulties presented by invisibility are small and in return you get &quot;I'M INVISIBLE! WOO!&quot;. I mean it's really cool to become one with the shadows. The difficulties presented by Auspex 2 are large (i.e. people in this thread are talking about requiring entire city concepts to be used to deal with the issues it throws up) and in return you get &quot;I know if someone has committed a terrible crime or not&quot;. That's a bad bargain. And that's the difference between Auspex 2 and invisibility.<br /> <br /> It may not be a problem for everyone in this thread (and what is universally considered such?), but it's a big constraint for many of us. And I really don't think someone is a better GM than another because one wants a friendly seeming vampire to be a secret diablerist and the other wants the PCs to be her first ever victims. Maybe the first GM doesn't WANT their character to be the latter. Maybe the secret diablerist is what they want. The button is a big constraint and for some people that is legitimately going to be a problem and they're not wrong to say it is for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:18:55-07:00","id":974061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973987#post973987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it IS constraining to have an easily available &quot;I know you're guilty&quot; button in the game. That's undeniable because I list circumstances all day long that it constrains a GM or player from doing. &quot;I want my character to be a secret diablerist / sorry, it's not possible to keep diablerie secret&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with you that it is constraining. I don't view constraining as inherently less desirable, in fact it is my philosophy that things are better defined by limitations than by potential. I believe setting and characters shouldn't be haphazard patchwork ragamuffins divorced from one another but rather the two aspects of the story should be built using complimentary fabrics, stitched together with intention.<br /> <br /> As a storyteller you could, make a rare macguffen that's sought after by others and is handed down by the PC's sire upon letting the PC diablerize him. That's way more interest than every vampire is a secret diablerist because it is so easy to be a shut-in for just a little bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=973987#post973987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>The difficulties presented by invisibility are small</u> and in return you get &quot;I'M INVISIBLE! WOO!&quot;. I mean it's really cool to become one with the shadows. The difficulties presented by Auspex 2 are large (i.e. people in this thread are talking about requiring entire city concepts to be used to deal with the issues it throws up) and in return you get &quot;I know if someone has committed a terrible crime or not&quot;. That's a bad bargain. And that's the difference between Auspex 2 and invisibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <u>underlined emphasis</u> is mine. I am so sorry, it is too tempting to not get side tracked by the implied contention that knowing people can be invisible wouldn't completely change the dynamics of every person's life/unlife, especially when the people that know those invisible also happen to be inhuman blood-thirsty scheming grudge-holders that they have to interact/compete for resources with.<br /> <br /> If a domain gatherings and individual vampire's unlives (barring the most naive or uninformed neonates) don't account for the power of invisibility then they are portrayed poorly. This is the same scale as people just knowing your secrets, I mean what about Invisible witnesses to anything you do night from night? Also low level Auspex doesn't grant the ability to know where you sleep, or to ambush you horrifically. Knowing you could be being followed unless you use counter strategies or powers changes things a lot.<br /> <br /> Pretending the existence of Invisibility doesn't have far reaching consequences to turn someone else's argument into a seeming strawman is just plain inaccurate.<br /> <br /> Also instead of 1/5 Clans having access like Auspex, 2/5 Clans have access to Obfuscate which means the likelihood of being invisibly stalked is higher than people pulling your secrets from the ether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-21-2016, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:09:11-07:00","id":974085,"title":"","content":"All powers are &quot;problematic&quot; from one point of view or another. The problem is that people are trying to make an objective argument about something that is subjective.<br /> <br /> What I see here are people trying to black and white something that is 1000 shades of grey and black. A diablerist is not automatically a demented soul sucking monster. He is somebody that committed a terrible act. You should be wary of him, but then again you should be wary of any vampire, right?<br /> <br /> Truth and knowledge don\u00b4t always matter. Impotence in the face of stagnant procedure and social power dynamics are a facet of reality and are greatly present in standard vampiric society.<br /> <br /> And when truth and knowledge matter it doesn\u00b4t have to matter in a positive light. You could live terrified in the presence of people you know committed heinous acts that are punishable by law and yet there is nothing you can do about it.<br /> <br /> The game espouses a dark atmosphere.<br /> <br /> First idiot neonate that starts spilling the secrets of other vampires will soon learn when to leverage their knowledge when they can and shut the fuck up when they cannot. The ones that learn to tell the difference between the two (pray to the Lord), will be the ones most likely to keep existing. &quot;Like me so much that you been spying on me, eh little kitty? So, lets get to know each other better.&quot;<br /> <br /> The self-righteous and judgemental will soon isolate themselves in a society where, by default, all are bloodsucking predaory unholy abominations. Careful not to be left alone in the dark. There ARE monsters under the bed.<br /> <br /> There isno objective value in thinking that players being able to detect dark secrets is more &quot;constraining&quot; than them being able to turn invisible.<br /> <br /> Why are people trying to establish something as universely &quot;constraining&quot;? There is no such thing. Aplples and oranges, sorbets and juices.<br /> <br /> Any Discipline can be plot jarring depending on the plot. There is nothing wrong with that. Either rethink the plot in question or adjust the power so that it isn\u00b4t able to disrupt the plot.<br /> <br /> The use of a discrete power is a narrative statement. Narrative statements are a building block of storytelling. There are no &quot;better&quot; one than the other. Each and everyone one eliminates countless stories.<br /> <br /> Being given advice on how you might let the power be and still keep suspense on a plot is not being &quot;told to ST better&quot;. It is just giving advice on how to keep suspense using the directives as written. Don\u00b4t like the advice, don\u00b4t use it. Don\u00b4t agree with it, and care to, discuss it. Don\u00b4t act like people are trying to put others down.<br /> <br /> Chipped shoulders and thin skins abound. But this is the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:53:12-07:00","id":982793,"title":"","content":"The problem that I see with Auspex becoming an infallible &quot;have you ever&quot; game, is that what the players can do, so too can the NPCs.<br /> <br /> This would make the Court Truthsayer a standard fixture in every prince's court. All he has to do is call up anyone he dislikes and ask &quot;have you ever...&quot;, and then he is free to mete out whatever &quot;justice&quot; he wishes, worry free.<br /> <br /> By moving away from patterns and auras into directed questions, every vampire with any subordinates now has to have a Truthsayer handy. And if they are particularly paranoid, forget the Truthsayer and learn Auspex for themselves.<br /> <br /> &quot;Have you been disloyal to me?&quot; That becomes the most feared question of all. And under the new Auspex mechanics, it damns almost all of the damned all over again.<br /> <br /> But it does give rise to the notion of a new bloodline for Truthsayers....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T03:17:33-07:00","id":983234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=982793#post982793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would make the Court Truthsayer a standard fixture in every prince's court. All he has to do is call up anyone he dislikes and ask &quot;have you ever...&quot;, and then he is free to mete out whatever &quot;justice&quot; he wishes, worry free.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would, of course, make him the World's Biggest Target\u2122.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T03:32:17-07:00","id":983235,"title":"","content":"Really, Auspex shouldn't be the end of an investigation, but the beginning. You can ask if someone is a diablerist or ever killed a kindred or killed a specific kindred but then it's a matter of using that information as well as possibly confirming it in other ways. And by using it I don't specifically mean accuse the kindred in question. That information could be leverage or have some other use to a third party.<br /> <br /> Other vampires won't necessarily argue that Auspex on its own can't be believed, but the standing of the kindred doing the reading, as well as the accused, as well as other agendas may determine how seriously such accusations might be taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T05:33:05-07:00","id":983263,"title":"","content":"Auspex as Clues for the Investigation system! That would be so much fun. And you could cash them in for social bonuses, which is right up with Vampire's social focus!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:00:53-07:00","id":983648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=982793#post982793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem that I see with Auspex becoming an infallible &quot;have you ever&quot; game, is that what the players can do, so too can the NPCs.<br /> <br /> This would make the Court Truthsayer a standard fixture in every prince's court. All he has to do is call up anyone he dislikes and ask &quot;have you ever...&quot;, and then he is free to mete out whatever &quot;justice&quot; he wishes, worry free.<br /> <br /> By moving away from patterns and auras into directed questions, every vampire with any subordinates now has to have a Truthsayer handy. And if they are particularly paranoid, forget the Truthsayer and learn Auspex for themselves.<br /> <br /> &quot;Have you been disloyal to me?&quot; That becomes the most feared question of all. And under the new Auspex mechanics, it damns almost all of the damned all over again.<br /> <br /> But it does give rise to the notion of a new bloodline for Truthsayers....</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd think that what happen to Sultans who put too much trust and power in the hands of Jafar would be a lesson learned by all of us by the time we finished watching Aladdin.<br /> <br /> Alas, it isn't so...<br /> <br /> On a less acid note;<br /> <br /> The general notion that a vampire acts immediately and decisively on every bit of information that it comes upon is a misunderstanding of a short lived blood bag. Vampires are ever living vicious schemers, even more so the ones that come to hold &quot;temporal&quot; power in their society. They will use your secrets to make you useful to them. A vampire is a powerful servant and a smart ruler will only sentence one to death if it furthers a goal worth the loss of opportunity.<br /> <br /> The naivete that comprise notions of honor, loyalty and ethics cedes place to lies, deceptions and opportunism very early in a vampire's unlife. Specially one that participates in the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> Rulers that don't acknowledge this will soon find themselves devoid of followers or turned to ash.<br /> <br /> My guess is that you have to be extremely powerful to pull off being the smothering mother kind of ruler. Very powerful. Like yuuuuuge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T07:33:14-07:00","id":986750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=972887#post972887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is basically how I intend to run it. The tainted condition is kind of meaningless if diablerists are detectable as diablerists long after the condition has been resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree, it defeats the purpose of the Tainted Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T07:49:13-07:00","id":986760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=986750#post986750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I agree, it defeats the purpose of the Tainted Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the purpose of the Tainted Condition is to give you a penalty to a dice pool equal to the victim's Blood Potency once per chapter, and to give you a Beat when it resolves. In fact, I'm pretty sure that is literally all it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T07:51:12-07:00","id":986762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=986760#post986760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure the purpose of the Tainted Condition is to give you a penalty to a dice pool equal to the victim's Blood Potency once per chapter, and to give you a Beat when it resolves. In fact, I'm pretty sure that is literally all it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, when I made the quoted post I misremembered what the tainted condition was. <i>Now</i> I have no issues with Auspex detecting Diablerie at any time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T20:14:30-07:00","id":987073,"title":"","content":"A question like &quot;Is this person a diablerist&quot; would not give you a simple yes answer in second edition. Auspex in 2nd edition is giving your beast's reaction to a question. Each kindred's beast is different and will probably give a different reaction. So two vampires with Auspex will likely perceive a diablerist differently. Hence, its unreliable evidence to condemn someone for a crime. However, there is a ritual for compelling the truth that a prince could demand. One should also find out who the victim was since there can't be a crime like diablerie would a murder. It could set up a nice quest to prove (or disprove) a claim of diablerie. But Auspex alone should be the first and final say on any question.<br /> <br /> Diablerie is a dangerous act that should be very hard to get away with or else you will have certain players trying to commit it all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 10-13-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T03:07:08-07:00","id":987166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987073#post987073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question like &quot;Is this person a diablerist&quot; would not give you a simple yes answer in second edition. Auspex in 2nd edition is giving your beast's reaction to a question.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Discipline says that the answer should be conveyed with imagery and gives examples of how the storyteller can be atmospheric in describing the answer, but I don't think it's a licence to refuse to answer a player's question on a Success. It suggests things like answering the question &quot;who here is most afraid&quot; with the individual in question smelling of urine or making whimpering sounds. Not &quot;a jaundiced yellow light gathers around one corner of the room where three people stand&quot;. Both are descriptive, but one answers the question and one refuses to. No, you don't hear a GM's voice saying &quot;Yes&quot;, but that seems to be just an attempt to be immersive, not to take away from the efficacy of the power.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Auspex 1 has to be (as written) one of the most abusable powers in the game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:50:53-07:00","id":987193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987166#post987166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Discipline says that the answer should be conveyed with imagery and gives examples of how the storyteller can be atmospheric in describing the answer, but I don't think it's a licence to refuse to answer a player's question on a Success. It suggests things like answering the question &amp;quot;who here is most afraid&amp;quot; with the individual in question smelling of urine or making whimpering sounds. Not &amp;quot;a jaundiced yellow light gathers around one corner of the room where three people stand&amp;quot;. Both are descriptive, but one answers the question and one refuses to. No, you don't hear a GM's voice saying &amp;quot;Yes&amp;quot;, but that seems to be just an attempt to be immersive, not to take away from the efficacy of the power.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Auspex 1 has to be (as written) one of the most abusable powers in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree! On a success the GM must answer providing an immage that &quot;answers&quot; to the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T06:56:23-07:00","id":987233,"title":"","content":"I'm running kindred law and order game and I'm looking for ways Kindred can hide crimes from Kindred Judges with high Aupex. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:02:57-07:00","id":987237,"title":"","content":"Resolve + Blood Potency counters Lay Open the Mind. Uncanny Perception doesn't really do biography questions. And the Spirit's Touch can be countered by destroying or hiding objects.<br /> <br /> 'I was Dominated,' is a pretty easy excuse that's hard to disprove regarding specific situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:25:10-07:00","id":987247,"title":"","content":"You can't hide a crime because nothing stops Auspex. Getting away with a crime has nothing to do with concealing it and everything to do with the criminal's value to the regime. If the domain is governed by fiat, then it's a matter of the criminal's value to whoever makes the decision of guilt or innocence. If it's a matter where evidence is required, Auspex also tells the user where to find it or what they need, and it is simply a matter of whether or not proof has to be legally obtained to be admissable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:55:39-07:00","id":987254,"title":"","content":"I didn't say the GM could avoid answering the question. My point is that every vampire would see something slightly different with Auspex. How someone perceive fear through auspex can and should be different between players. In short, the power is as abusable as you wish it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:00:53-07:00","id":987257,"title":"","content":"I hate to open this can of worms again, but Auspex can only be verified by other Auspex users, which puts it into the same category as eyewitness testimony. Which is to say, unreliable evidence on its own, but a good reason to start looking for more concrete evidence. How your Kindred Court handles it is of course up to you as ST, but I would have most Kindred be hesitant to admit Auspex accounts as evidence, not the least of which because they know it could just as easily be used against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:05:26-07:00","id":987260,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can really call it abuse if you're using a power precisely for its intended function. Is it an incredibly useful power? Yes. That's a feature, not a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:18:46-07:00","id":987262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987260#post987260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can really call it abuse if you're using a power precisely for its intended function. Is it an incredibly useful power? Yes. That's a feature, not a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is it a feature of Auspex to have it be the be all, end all of any investigation? Did you commit this crime? Yes? End of story. That sounds like a very boring story. I'm not disputing the power of auspex but rather what its effect should be on an investigation. Auspex shouldn't be the solo evidence used to condemn criminals or its going to make a for a very boring trial story. And proving or disproving guilt in a kindred trail can make for a very fun storyline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 10-14-2016, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:55:42-07:00","id":987278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987262#post987262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it a feature of Auspex to have it be the be all, end all of any investigation?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not. It's the start of an investigation. You found out someone is guilty of a crime, but you have nothing but your word against theirs to prove it, same as if you witnessed a murder but had no proof to show for it. A lot of thrillers start off that way. Granted, other Auspex users can corroborate your claims just as other eyewitnesses can but it's still not hard evidence. And we're talking about vampires here. Creatures paranoid to no end, and intrinsically self-serving. You think anyone is going to back you up without a little quid-pro-quo? You think anyone is going to take you on your word when your word could just as easily condemn them? Everyone in the Domain is guilty of <i>something</i>, who gets popped for what has more to do with politics than actual guilt. You want to catch your culprit, you're going to need better leverage than &quot;my spirit senses told me&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987262#post987262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you commit this crime? Yes? End of story.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, unless the crime is specifically Diablerie, that's not a question I'd allow with Auspex. Second of all, for the reasons given above, no, not end of story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987262#post987262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a very boring story. I'm not disputing the power of auspex but rather what its effect should be on an investigation. Auspex shouldn't be the solo evidence used to condemn criminals or its going to make a for a very boring trial story. And proving or disproving guilt in a kindred trail can make for a very fun storyline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Auspex shouldn't be the solo evidence used to condemn criminals because that would be stupid. It would be comparable to human courts condemning criminals solely on the basis of eyewitness testimony. Which, as I've said before, is how you end up with witch hunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T09:11:19-07:00","id":987290,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I agree with you, I wasn't so much responding to you as to others in this topic on how they seem to believe a prince could just use Auspex and condemn people for crimes. I like the analogy of Auspex being like eyewitness testimony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","user":"Wissenschaft","date":". 10-14-2016, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:16:59-07:00","id":987339,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate. Lots and lots of Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:21:47-07:00","id":987341,"title":"","content":"If the tainted condition gradually disappears over a number of months equal to the blood potency of the victim, would auspex on its own be unable to make the determination that a particular vampire diablerized someone once the tainted condition wears off?<br /> <br /> Of course asking the diablerist if they had committed the act would allow for auspex to pickup on their lying. That is unless they have forgotten their diablerie through the fog of torpor or perhaps a memory hole induced by Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:27:34-07:00","id":987343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987278#post987278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not. It's the start of an investigation. You found out someone is guilty of a crime, but you have nothing but your word against theirs to prove it,</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is fine if that is the adventure you wish to run, but immediately creates major headaches if you want to run a wide variety of other archetypal adventures such as a murder mystery. Want to have PCs in doubt as whether someone is a villain or not, know whether their new ally is a traitor or not, basically any adventure where not knowing if someone is X or not, becomes much more difficult to pull off. An adventure where you know someone is guilty but have to convince others could be a very fun adventure. But it doesn't alter that Auspex 1 as written constrains the sort of adventures you can run a lot. No more whodunnits for you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987278#post987278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">same as if you witnessed a murder but had no proof to show for it. A lot of thrillers start off that way. Granted, other Auspex users can corroborate your claims just as other eyewitnesses can but it's still not hard evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, we're back to the constraints on the stories you can tell. You presume a setting where there's some rigorous legal process amongst the vampire community or that the person who sees it has to prove beyond doubt to others that it is the case. The powerful prince whose word is law is a staple of Vampire games. If they have Auspex 1 (not a big ask), job done. They pronounce that the new vampire is a diablerist. Doesn't even have to be a powerful prince. Anyone whom others either trust enough or don't wish to challenge will do. If Diablerie is this terrible crime then simply having elders able to spot it is sufficient to bring down punishment. You don't have to have punishments or problems imposed by community consensus. If Diablerie is this unforgiveable crime then simply having random powerful elder know you're guilty of it is sufficient to invite destruction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987278#post987278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we're talking about vampires here. Creatures paranoid to no end, and intrinsically self-serving. You think anyone is going to back you up without a little quid-pro-quo? You think anyone is going to take you on your word when your word could just as easily condemn them? Everyone in the Domain is guilty of <i>something</i>, who gets popped for what has more to do with politics than actual guilt. You want to catch your culprit, you're going to need better leverage than &quot;my spirit senses told me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting &quot;my spirit senses told me&quot; in quotes as if it would be treated in-game the same way people would treat it in real life is disingenuous. A lot of vampires have those senses and experience them intimately and even those that don't know that they are real. Furthermore, others can verify. Any remotely respectable vampire saying someone was guilty of such a terrible crime would get the others all gathering together to check for themselves. And when they all agreed, job done. Either Diablerie is not this terrible crime that other vampires all find repugnant, or you don't make it easy to detect. Anything other than this leads to action against the diablerist. I don't have to get on with my neighbour to help them deal with someone who is eating people on our street.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987278#post987278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First of all, unless the crime is specifically Diablerie, that's not a question I'd allow with Auspex. Second of all, for the reasons given above, no, not end of story.</div> </div> </div> </div>The write-up of the power offers a wide range of options beyond just Diablerie. As written it could very well tell you whether someone is guilty of other crimes. In fact as written it should.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987278#post987278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. Auspex shouldn't be the solo evidence used to condemn criminals because that would be stupid. It would be comparable to human courts condemning criminals solely on the basis of eyewitness testimony. Which, as I've said before, is how you end up with witch hunts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And are human courts comparable to vampire society? If you're a community of a 100, most of whom have met each other and who organise themselves by who has the most power, witness testimony (what this effectively is) is going to be a common approach. Especially when a sizeable portion of your community (quite possibly including yourself) can become witnesses on request and the judge / ruler / police can also be witnesses.<br /> <br /> You can certainly build settings and adventures where the ability to easily detect Diablerie is not a problem. But it certainly limits a number of popular settings and adventures from being viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:31:20-07:00","id":987346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the tainted condition gradually disappears over a number of months equal to the blood potency of the victim, would auspex on its own be unable to make the determination that a particular vampire diablerized someone once the tainted condition wears off?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the question we have been debating for the past 6 pages. Honestly, it seems very odd to me, since the example question is &quot;is this person a diablerist?&quot;, not &quot;does this person have the Tainted Condition?&quot; and there is nothing at all in the book that suggests the Tainted Condition would be the source of Diablerie aura stains. That said, I think it's a cool house rule with interesting implications if you do want to run it that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course asking the diablerist if they had committed the act would allow for auspex to pickup on their lying. That is unless they have forgotten their diablerie through the fog of torpor or perhaps a memory hole induced by Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether or not Auspex can detect lies is another point of contention, although not one that has gotten much focus in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:33:19-07:00","id":987348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987290#post987290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> I agree with you, I wasn't so much responding to you as to others in this topic on how they seem to believe a prince could just use Auspex and condemn people for crimes. I like the analogy of Auspex being like eyewitness testimony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some princes can. And even if they can't, just having the prince know you're guilty is sufficient to start them getting whatever they do need to deal with you. It's not that having this stops all types of story or setting. It's that it causes major problems with a number of popular types of story or setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:40:24-07:00","id":987350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987346#post987346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not Auspex can detect lies is another point of contention, although not one that has gotten much focus in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the wording says &quot;allows to ask a question&quot; and the examples cover things such as knowing someone's intent (&quot;Who is about to attack me?&quot;), value judgements (&quot;Who is weakest&quot;), inanimate objects (&quot;what is most dangerous here?&quot; example answer: &quot;a car crusher&quot;), mental state (&quot;Who is most afraid?&quot;), probability (several of the previous). There are no explicit limitations on the power as written and the examples show it to be able to access multiple categories of information and be sophisticated enough to make logical comparisons between them. I'd say lying is definitely a contender for a legitimate question.<br /> <br /> I think the <i>intent</i> of the rule is to be limited to fear / threat questions and for judgements to be based around the user's own mental processes (&quot;I find the car crusher more dangerous than the police officer&quot;). But it really needs some tightening up to actually reflect that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:45:30-07:00","id":987354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987257#post987257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to open this can of worms again, but Auspex can only be verified by other Auspex users, which puts it into the same category as eyewitness testimony. Which is to say, unreliable evidence on its own, but a good reason to start looking for more concrete evidence. How your Kindred Court handles it is of course up to you as ST, but I would have most Kindred be hesitant to admit Auspex accounts as evidence, not the least of which because they know it could just as easily be used against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this thread overlaps rather too much with the Diablerie and Auspex thread and could do with a merge if such things are done here, but I'll reply here as well. There's an important difference between Auspex and eye-witness testimony. Eye witness testimony is limited by happenstance and you have to hope you get a suitable set of eye-witnesses. Auspex can add eye-witnesses as needed (in theory) and the pool of them is likely to be a significant portion of your community. You can also draft in respected eye-witnesses post-fact as well. And eye-witness testimony is not a weak thing even in our world. People are routinely convicted from eye-witness testimony. Let alone when you can keep adding further eye-witnesses to see if they agree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\"><i>Fnord!</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11763-knasser","name":"knasser","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11763_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:56:04-07:00","id":987357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>knasser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987343#post987343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is fine if that is the adventure you wish to run, but immediately creates major headaches if you want to run a wide variety of other archetypal adventures such as a murder mystery. Want to have PCs in doubt as whether someone is a villain or not, know whether their new ally is a traitor or not, basically any adventure where not knowing if someone is X or not, becomes much more difficult to pull off. An adventure where you know someone is guilty but have to convince others could be a very fun adventure. But it doesn't alter that Auspex 1 as written constrains the sort of adventures you can run a lot. No more whodunnits for you!</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally every power constrains what kind of stories you can tell when you have characters with them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, we're back to the constraints on the stories you can tell. You presume a setting where there's some rigorous legal process amongst the vampire community or that the person who sees it has to prove beyond doubt to others that it is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume a setting where executing vampires is not taken lightly. What kind of legal processes are involved can vary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The powerful prince whose word is law is a staple of Vampire games. If they have Auspex 1 (not a big ask), job done. They pronounce that the new vampire is a diablerist. Doesn't even have to be a powerful prince. Anyone whom others either trust enough or don't wish to challenge will do. If Diablerie is this terrible crime then simply having elders able to spot it is sufficient to bring down punishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if the <i>other</i> elders are comfortable allowing them that kind of power. Which, if they have a modicum of self-interest, they should not. If the prince can condemn anyone to death without question simply by pronouncing them a diablerist, he'd better be extremely secure in his power, or he's going to have people who fear him falsely accusing them (read: everyone who doesn't stand to gain by keeping him in power) out for a coup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to have punishments or problems imposed by community consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a sense you do, because if the community doesn't consent, at least by complacency, to the way punishments are metted out, they will rebel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Diablerie is this unforgiveable crime then simply having random powerful elder know you're guilty of it is sufficient to invite destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if the other elders don't fear him having that power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting &amp;quot;my spirit senses told me&amp;quot; in quotes as if it would be treated in-game the same way people would treat it in real life is disingenuous. A lot of vampires have those senses and experience them intimately and even those that don't know that they are real.</div> </div> </div> </div>I put it in quotes to indicate that it was a quotation, not as a mark of irony. Of course vampires wouldn't doubt that such powers are real, just as humans don't doubt that people can visually witness crimes. What they <i>would</i> have reason to doubt is the reliability, intentions, and legitimacy of those who claim to have those powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore, others can verify. Any remotely respectable vampire saying someone was guilty of such a terrible crime would get the others all gathering together to check for themselves. And when they all agreed, job done. Either Diablerie is not this terrible crime that other vampires all find repugnant, or you don't make it easy to detect. Anything other than this leads to action against the diablerist. I don't have to get on with my neighbour to help them deal with someone who is eating people on our street.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only other Auspex users can verify their claims, just as only other eyewitnesses can verify eyewitness accounts. If your Domain is comfortable condemning Kindred to death on the basis of testimony alone, without objective evidence... well, then it's much more liberal with the death penalty than any Domain I would run. That doesn't stop vililanteism, but that is also taken as an incredibly serious crime in the Requim I read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The write-up of the power offers a wide range of options beyond just Diablerie. As written it could very well tell you whether someone is guilty of other crimes. In fact as written it should.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* I disagree. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And are human courts comparable to vampire society? If you're a community of a 100, most of whom have met each other and who organise themselves by who has the most power, witness testimony (what this effectively is) is going to be a common approach. Especially when a sizeable portion of your community (quite possibly including yourself) can become witnesses on request and the judge / ruler / police can also be witnesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of comparison to eyewitness testimony is to compare the reliability of testimony, not the procedures of a court.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can certainly build settings and adventures where the ability to easily detect Diablerie is not a problem. But it certainly limits a number of popular settings and adventures from being viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, every power constrains the stories you can tell. Comic book writers often have to jump through hoops to tell the stories they want to tell around the powers the protagonists have at their disposal. You want to pose a physical threat to superman? Use Kryptonite. You want to run a diablerie mystery where the identity of the diablerist can't be verified with Auspex? Use an En. The superpower arms race is real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T12:10:28-07:00","id":987364,"title":"","content":"If auspex in 2nd edition is a hinderence to the type of story you want to tell then change it. No one is forced to rigidly follow the letter of the rules. Go back to first edition's auspex rules. I know I prefer first edition's clan weakness for Ventrue and Daeva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T13:37:05-07:00","id":987411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987341#post987341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the tainted condition gradually disappears over a number of months equal to the blood potency of the victim, would auspex on its own be unable to make the determination that a particular vampire diablerized someone once the tainted condition wears off?<br /> <br /> Of course asking the diablerist if they had committed the act would allow for auspex to pickup on their lying. That is unless they have forgotten their diablerie through the fog of torpor or perhaps a memory hole induced by Dominate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I covered this in an earlier post, but you can end the Tainted condition in the very same scene that you committed Diablerie. It seems weird for Auspex to be unable to detect a Diablerist who committed their crime five minutes ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:56:14-07:00","id":987495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987411#post987411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I covered this in an earlier post, but you can end the Tainted condition in the very same scene that you committed Diablerie. It seems weird for Auspex to be unable to detect a Diablerist who committed their crime five minutes ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finding a way to pawn off the Tainted Condition that quickly is exactly the sort of thing Dragons, Acolytes, and serial diablerists would do so why would it be weird? There's plenty of inconsistent mechanics like that which don't make sense when you look at context. A Daeva with level 1 of Majesty can walk in with blood on their clothes, a severed head in their ]ands, and not a single onlooker would dare to call the police because they wouldn't want to inconvenience the Daeva. A few seconds application of Auspex can instantly and irrevocably obliterate hours or months of memory alteration done by Dominate. <br /> <br /> This hypothetical Mekhet comes across someone sporting a lot of aggravated wounds and his first thought isn't to ascertain the potential of becoming similarly injured? Of course not. His first act is to check to ask his Beast if the injured party is a diablerist. I've played with some pretty blatant meta gamers trying to use completely OOC knowledge of mechanics to justify having IC knowledge they shouldn't but that's a good one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:50:27-07:00","id":987513,"title":"","content":"You can learn the same information with Dominate.<br /> *meets gaze* &quot;Answer me truthfully; have you ever committed Diablerie?&quot;<br /> If anything, Dominate is worse because it can be performed with the response in full view of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:54:02-07:00","id":987515,"title":"","content":"Your argument is that it's okay because players can metagame their way around it? Seriously?<br /> <br /> And they don't have to sport &quot;a lot&quot; of aggravated wounds. It can be as low as a single wound.<br /> <br /> If a Vampire diablerized someone an hour ago and a PC uses Auspex to determine whether they are a Diablerist and the Storyteller says &quot;no,&quot; then the Storyteller is lying and betraying the trust of the PCs. Taking away something that the PCs have invested in (in this case, the ability to discover secrets) to protect your story over the PCs fun is bad form.<br /> <br /> I get that this sort of adversarial mindset of DM vs PCs is not uncommon, but I don't think it's in the spirit of the Storyteller system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:01:15-07:00","id":987608,"title":"","content":"Not sure if it helps at all, but in 1E I had a house-ruled merit that could hide the effects of diablerie on your aura. It took a lot of practice with a mixture of Auspex and Obfuscate. My character had come up with it as he was trying to appear as normal as possible (transferred over when 2E came out, with Protean and Obfuscate, he didn't even look like a Vampire according to his aura). Could something like that not be done with auspex now (bury that knowledge deep within your psyche) or dominate (sets a trigger to auto-flee if someone asks about it). Of course it would need to be done by another kindred (unless you house-rule in self-dominate), which could cause issues on their own, but a contested action might reveal the truth?<br /> <br /> And yes I know that technically anything can be house-ruled in, but I also prefer not to completely eliminate aspects of the RAW. Just, make it more difficult for them to find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:13:09-07:00","id":987637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987513#post987513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can learn the same information with Dominate.<br /> *meets gaze* &quot;Answer me truthfully; have you ever committed Diablerie?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>*rolls successful resist check* 'No.'<br /> <br /> Not to mention the other antics you could get up to. If some jumped up court is going to decide to terminate your potential immortality why not do whatever it took to weasel out of it? Have a friend Dominate you into forgetting what you did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T06:05:19-07:00","id":987715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=987515#post987515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your argument is that it's okay because players can metagame their way around it? Seriously?<br /> <br /> And they don't have to sport &quot;a lot&quot; of aggravated wounds. It can be as low as a single wound.<br /> <br /> If a Vampire diablerized someone an hour ago and a PC uses Auspex to determine whether they are a Diablerist and the Storyteller says &quot;no,&quot; then the Storyteller is lying and betraying the trust of the PCs. Taking away something that the PCs have invested in (in this case, the ability to discover secrets) to protect your story over the PCs fun is bad form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see... so, for you, it's okay for PLAYERS to develop homebrew abilites to circumvent powers, but if a storyteller does it, they're mean and treacherous. Because they can't possibly have a storyline specific reason to have the power not working. Spare me the melodrama. The time investment a storyteller puts into designing and presenting a chronicle, coordinating enough time to play for all participants is NOT worth far less than the two dots allocated to a discipline written down on a character sheet by some one who just showed up because they're in town for the weekend and doesn't even take the time to outline a character background. The fact that they ruined the investigation storyline planned out for everyone else who doesn't use Auspex as a gun to the storyteller's head is not inconsequential.<br /> <br /> And no, my argument that because players can meta game around it doesn't make it okay. My argument is the line &quot;it's a feature, not a bug&quot; that's used to justify Auspex's accuracy and ability to undermine other players' &quot;fun&quot; is equally applicable when players find a loophole to undermine Auspex in a highly specific and unlikely scenario. Honestly, it kind of blows chunks that Auspex is the power designed to always auto-win in paper-rock-scissors and is available cost-free to only one fifth of the clans and has no equally potent counter or cost to use. So I have no qualms about stepping around it on occasion or letting players devise their own methods of giving the finger to the meta gaming player who arrived on the scene after the fact and instantly reverts to Auspex to instantly know everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T07:05:16-07:00","id":987729,"title":"","content":"I wonder if all these people complaining actually had a story &quot;ruined&quot; by a use of Auspex. If discovering one secret (that involves danger or weakness) ruins your plot and leaves you with no good recourse to keep the story going that is a poor story structure that lacks adaptability. <br /> <br /> Auspex 1 is about predatory danger and weakness, yet the people who complain it is too broad just choose to take a broad interpretation of what that means, probably to spite themselves and hype themselves to keep arguing over this. People just tend to overvalue information and :truth&quot; without social context. Social context is paramount to the standard Vampire game.<br /> <br /> This is probably the endless white rooming and needing to win the internet. I don't see any new arguments that weren't discussed to a reasonable length and shown that the power is fine. You don't like it, change it. Like any other power in the book.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T07:53:11-07:00","id":987749,"title":"","content":"Yes, some people do have stories that are derailed by an unforseen use of divination abilities. And there are some STs who are unable to adapt a story in the heat of the moment. Everyone has different playstyles. And I think that's really the heart of the problem - this isn't endless &quot;white-rooming&quot; but examples extrapolated from personal experiences. However, because everyone has different playstyles, we don't necessarily see &quot;eye to eye&quot; on the matter, in no small part due to the problem of the internet being hard to read intent. And when people's playstyles are being insulted or disparaged, then its not hard to respond with a bit of bile back. I admit, that's what happened with me earlier. <br /> <br /> Anyways, the point is that so much of the use of these abilities depend on the context of the game. And that context changes from table to table in some rather extrodinary ways and some subtle but critical ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:25:32-07:00","id":987792,"title":"","content":"In what way does Auspex always win at Rock Paper Scissors? What are Rock and Paper in this analogy? I don't see any Rock Paper Scissors game going on in Vampire unless you're talking about it literally in Masquerade LARP.<br /> <br /> What Auspex does is give information. It's a pretty reliable information gathering power, but information is only as useful as you make it. Auspex doesn't give you any special means of <i>using</i> that information to your advantage. You have to play the political game to leverage your Auspex-acquired information, and at that point you're engaging with the primary external conflict of Requiem. Power working as intended.<br /> <br /> It's also far from the most effective information gathering power in CofD. Auspex is peanuts to Mage Sight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T06:11:23-07:00","id":988220,"title":"","content":"Its a bit unfair to compare Auspex to Mage - not only is Mage specifically designed to be more powerful than most other supernaturals, but mages as a whole literally specialize in gathering knowledge. And its also a bit difficult to make that appearance - there are 10 flavors of Mage Sight, after all, that do vastly different things, and we can only assume a given mage will have access to 1/3rd of those Sights, and only one at a time. <br /> <br /> Auspex compared to mortal psychic merits, demonic powers, Advanced merits / Mirmir's Wisdom, a handful of divination Contracts and werewolf Knowledge / Insight Gifts actually matches up fairly well. In fact, I personally find that Auspex, when combined with Kindred Sense merits and Cruac's divination rituals, is actually on the stronger side when compared to most other 2e supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-16-2016, 09:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T08:06:06-07:00","id":988251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=988220#post988220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a bit unfair to compare Auspex to Mage - not only is Mage specifically designed to be more powerful than most other supernaturals, but mages as a whole literally specialize in gathering knowledge. And its also a bit difficult to make that appearance - there are 10 flavors of Mage Sight, after all, that do vastly different things, and we can only assume a given mage will have access to 1/3rd of those Sights, and only one at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=988220#post988220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex compared to mortal psychic merits, demonic powers, Advanced merits / Mirmir's Wisdom, a handful of divination Contracts and werewolf Knowledge / Insight Gifts actually matches up fairly well. In fact, I personally find that Auspex, when combined with Kindred Sense merits and Cruac's divination rituals, is actually on the stronger side when compared to most other 2e supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Asking questions of the ST and getting symbolic imagery in answer is pretty much the standard for information gathering powers in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T12:46:26-07:00","id":988344,"title":"","content":"Mekhet also literally specialize in gathering secrets, which is why I find arbitrarily removing that ability to be a little strange and a lot undesirable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T04:14:06-07:00","id":988780,"title":"","content":"If Obfuscate can hide the beast from Auspex, would it, or at least a devotion, not also be able to hide diablerie from Auspex. Could it not also be developed, through devotions, to hide just about anything (lies, murders, etc.) from the powers of Auspex?<br /> <br /> One maxim that I would think applies aptly to the wanton use of Auspex is &quot;You can't ID, what you can't see&quot;.<br /> <br /> At that point, the only Rocks, Paper, Scissors game would be the clash of wills, neh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10978-azenogoth","name":"Azenogoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10978_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:20:11-07:00","id":988914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=988780#post988780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Obfuscate can hide the beast from Auspex, would it, or at least a devotion, not also be able to hide diablerie from Auspex. Could it not also be developed, through devotions, to hide just about anything (lies, murders, etc.) from the powers of Auspex?</div> </div> </div> </div>At ST discretion, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:19:24-07:00","id":988943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azenogoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=988780#post988780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Obfuscate can hide the beast from Auspex, would it, or at least a devotion, not also be able to hide diablerie from Auspex. Could it not also be developed, through devotions, to hide just about anything (lies, murders, etc.) from the powers of Auspex?<br /> <br /> One maxim that I would think applies aptly to the wanton use of Auspex is &quot;You can't ID, what you can't see&quot;.<br /> <br /> At that point, the only Rocks, Paper, Scissors game would be the clash of wills, neh?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Doesn't Auspex specifically state it can break through Obfuscate? Any devotion that you would create to hide something from Auspex would just create a clash of wills because it's two opposing disciplines... Wouldn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:40:56-07:00","id":988955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/971363-diablerie-and-auspex?p=988943#post988943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Doesn't Auspex specifically state it can break through Obfuscate? Any devotion that you would create to hide something from Auspex would just create a clash of wills because it's two opposing disciplines... Wouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 125, Clash of Wills, states all conflicting powers triggers a Clash of Wills. This explicitly extends to Devotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}